WEBVTT

1
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.124
What is love?

2
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:46.749
Love? Love is life.

3
00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:49.582
Love? What is love?

4
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.665
Why and where?

5
00:00:52.916 --> 00:00:57.249
I believe that God predetermined
all our emotional relationships.

6
00:00:57.916 --> 00:00:59.790
But He left it to us
to find each other.

7
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.499
He made us all couples...

8
00:01:02.916 --> 00:01:05.665
...and each one has a soul mate.

9
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:08.582
A soul mate? What nonsense!

10
00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:10.332
I don't believe in all this...

11
00:01:10.958 --> 00:01:15.290
I'm absolutely sure. Somewhere,
someone has been made for me...

12
00:01:16.291 --> 00:01:19.290
...and that someday,
I shall certainly meet him.

13
00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:21.665
Okay, but will someone
please tell me...

14
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.957
...how would I know
who was made for me?

15
00:01:24.041 --> 00:01:27.665
I mean, will she be holding
a placard with my name on it?

16
00:01:27.791 --> 00:01:31.124
When I see her,
will there be a clap of thunder...

17
00:01:31.208 --> 00:01:32.832
...or a flash of lightning? What?

18
00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:34.665
How would I recognise her?

19
00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:38.040
I don't know what others would do,
but I'll certainly know it's him.

20
00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:40.332
He will tell me...

21
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:44.624
He will give me a sign, and
my heart would know it's him.

22
00:01:45.958 --> 00:01:48.207
What is all this?
- This is love.

23
00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.415
Love?

24
00:02:00.916 --> 00:02:06.957
"However far apart they may be..."

25
00:02:07.541 --> 00:02:10.207
"Their paths will meet,
come what may."

26
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:13.832
"When two people are
made for each other."

27
00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:17.415
"Made for each other."

28
00:02:40.916 --> 00:02:47.374
"Like the heart and heartbeats...
- Made for each other."

29
00:02:47.541 --> 00:02:53.999
"Like the eye and the mirror...
- Made for each other."

30
00:02:54.125 --> 00:03:00.540
"Like the monsoon and the rains...
- Made for each other."

31
00:03:00.875 --> 00:03:07.165
"There's a man for every woman...
- Made for each other."

32
00:03:07.541 --> 00:03:14.332
"Made for each other"

33
00:03:27.458 --> 00:03:30.915
"When God made a heart..."

34
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.707
"...He split it in two."

35
00:03:34.166 --> 00:03:37.790
"He gave them two names..."

36
00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:40.790
"...Radha and Krishna"

37
00:03:40.916 --> 00:03:44.290
"Now the two hearts beat."

38
00:03:44.333 --> 00:03:47.082
"They part and they unite."

39
00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:50.749
"For they are made for each other."

40
00:03:50.916 --> 00:04:03.957
"Made for each other."

41
00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:08.749
"I didn't get an inkling when..."

42
00:05:09.208 --> 00:05:12.915
"...furtively, like a thief..."

43
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.290
"I didn't get an inkling when..."

44
00:05:24.666 --> 00:05:27.915
"...furtively, like a thief..."

45
00:05:28.041 --> 00:05:32.124
"...the first look of love..."

46
00:05:32.416 --> 00:05:35.582
"...stole my heart away."

47
00:05:36.291 --> 00:05:40.290
"Stole my heart away."

48
00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:51.332
"I didn't get an inkling when..."

49
00:05:51.666 --> 00:05:55.082
"...furtively, like a thief..."

50
00:05:55.208 --> 00:05:59.207
"...the first look of love..."

51
00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:02.707
"...stole my heart away."

52
00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:07.040
"Stole my heart away."

53
00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:11.707
"Stole my heart away"

54
00:06:53.583 --> 00:07:15.874
"In the hide-n-seek
of my first love..."

55
00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:23.582
"...I took refuge in the shelter
of his eyes without a thought."

56
00:07:24.083 --> 00:07:27.749
"Now I'm frightened..."

57
00:07:28.416 --> 00:07:31.749
"...because furtively,
like a thief..."

58
00:07:31.916 --> 00:07:35.832
"...the first look of love..."

59
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.332
"...stole my heart away"

60
00:07:39.875 --> 00:07:48.832
"Stole my heart away"

61
00:08:17.458 --> 00:08:40.957
"My hair dishevelled, my gait
uncertain as if I were drunk."

62
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:48.582
"Were I seen, it would
raise a million questions."

63
00:08:49.166 --> 00:08:53.124
"Oh, how do I go home?"

64
00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:56.832
"...for furtively, like a thief..."

65
00:08:56.958 --> 00:09:00.749
"...the first look of love..."

66
00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:04.499
"...stole my heart away"

67
00:09:05.041 --> 00:09:13.249
"Stole my heart away"

68
00:09:20.625 --> 00:09:24.165
"I didn't get an inkling when..."

69
00:09:24.541 --> 00:09:27.874
"...furtively, like a thief..."

70
00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.999
"...the first look of love..."

71
00:09:32.125 --> 00:09:35.540
"...stole my heart away."

72
00:09:35.666 --> 00:09:38.165
Jimmy, is Rahul at the entry point?
- No, Rahul's not here.

73
00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:39.332
What do you mean not there?

74
00:09:39.416 --> 00:09:42.082
He's supposed to enter in
two minutes. Find him, fast!

75
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:43.457
Oh, God. I'll be right back.

76
00:09:43.541 --> 00:09:47.707
"Stole my heart away"

77
00:09:47.791 --> 00:09:49.457
Shruti, did you find Rahul?
- No.

78
00:09:49.541 --> 00:09:55.624
"Stole my heart away."

79
00:10:01.750 --> 00:10:04.999
"I didn't get an inkling when..."

80
00:10:05.833 --> 00:10:09.582
"...furtively, like a thief..."

81
00:10:16.833 --> 00:10:20.415
"I didn't get an inkling when..."

82
00:10:21.083 --> 00:10:24.124
"...furtively, like a thief..."

83
00:10:24.583 --> 00:10:28.582
"The first glance of love..."

84
00:10:28.708 --> 00:10:48.540
"...stole my heart away."

85
00:10:59.333 --> 00:11:01.499
Yes, very good. Keep it up,
everyone. - Rahul...

86
00:11:01.625 --> 00:11:02.707
Rahul! I've told you
numerous times that...

87
00:11:02.791 --> 00:11:06.082
...you should be at the wing
five minutes before your entry.

88
00:11:06.208 --> 00:11:09.165
When you're not there, I start
fretting that you'll be late...

89
00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:11.165
I got this idea at the last minute

90
00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.707
And I thought that if I
shoot out on to the stage...

91
00:11:12.791 --> 00:11:14.540
...the audience will freak out,
and that's what happened.

92
00:11:14.625 --> 00:11:16.540
And anyway, there was no goof up.
What's the fuss all about?

93
00:11:16.833 --> 00:11:19.332
Look Rahul, I'm fed up
with your last minute entries.

94
00:11:19.458 --> 00:11:20.582
Hey Nisha, I'm the director.

95
00:11:20.666 --> 00:11:23.374
I can change whatever and
whenever I want, including you.

96
00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.749
Forget it. You'll never
find another dancer like me.

97
00:11:25.833 --> 00:11:27.832
I can get Shruti to dance
better than you. - Shut up!

98
00:11:28.083 --> 00:11:30.790
Nisha! Fight with him later.
It's time to go on stage.

99
00:11:30.875 --> 00:11:33.374
Take the mike.
- Go and tell Suppandi. - I'll tell.

100
00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:35.124
What?
- What?

101
00:11:35.291 --> 00:11:36.874
Okay everybody,
let's get the lights.

102
00:11:37.916 --> 00:11:38.999
Idiot.

103
00:11:57.833 --> 00:11:59.540
Thank you. Thank you very much.

104
00:12:00.041 --> 00:12:02.790
I'd like to thank you all on
behalf of the entire team...

105
00:12:02.875 --> 00:12:07.374
...for making this dance show a
huge success. Thank you so much.

106
00:12:07.583 --> 00:12:11.374
As you all know, this is
the last night of this show.

107
00:12:11.625 --> 00:12:17.790
However, I promise you that
we'll be back here in three months...

108
00:12:17.875 --> 00:12:20.790
...with a new story, new songs...

109
00:12:20.875 --> 00:12:24.540
...and a new name. Maya.

110
00:12:25.708 --> 00:12:30.082
Maya? - Yes, 'Maya' is the
name of our new dance show.

111
00:12:30.375 --> 00:12:33.124
Thank you very much everybody,
and good night to you.

112
00:12:41.708 --> 00:12:43.499
Cheers!

113
00:12:43.750 --> 00:12:46.499
Wonderful.
- We had good fun at the show.

114
00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.957
Hey, hang on a minute.

115
00:12:50.375 --> 00:12:54.207
Rahul, this new play 'Maya'...
What's it all about? Tell us.

116
00:12:54.291 --> 00:12:55.915
Tell us Rahul. Please.
- Get up.

117
00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.749
Tell us about it.
- Okay, okay.

118
00:12:58.666 --> 00:13:01.749
Maya.

119
00:13:03.833 --> 00:13:07.165
I don't know. - What?
- I don't know. - What is this?

120
00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:10.832
If you didn't know that,
then why did you tell everyone...

121
00:13:10.916 --> 00:13:12.832
...that we're doing a
new play called 'Maya'...

122
00:13:12.916 --> 00:13:14.999
...and that we'll do
it in three months?

123
00:13:15.125 --> 00:13:17.832
Now look, even I don't
know who or what Maya is...

124
00:13:17.916 --> 00:13:21.207
...but I do know that in three
months we'll do a play called 'Maya'.

125
00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:26.249
Do you have in mind a
girl who's like Maya?

126
00:13:27.291 --> 00:13:30.665
She's still in my imagination,
not in my mind.

127
00:13:35.041 --> 00:13:37.540
Nisha! I've got a girl in mind.

128
00:13:37.666 --> 00:13:40.415
Rahul! aren't you talking about
Pammi, the Colonel's daughter?

129
00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.332
Am I right? Isn't it Pammi?

130
00:13:42.416 --> 00:13:46.374
Rahul, is Maya the kind of
girl you can fall in love with?

131
00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.707
I don't fall in love with girls.

132
00:13:48.791 --> 00:13:50.707
Girls fall in love with me.
- There he goes again.

133
00:13:50.791 --> 00:13:55.082
But Maya is the kind of
girl that anyone could love.

134
00:13:59.375 --> 00:14:02.624
Maya is the kind of girl for
whom you would leave your Soni.

135
00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:06.832
You dare not cheat on my sister.
- Ballu, relax. Quite.

136
00:14:07.166 --> 00:14:08.832
What does she do?

137
00:14:10.666 --> 00:14:11.749
She comes in dreams.

138
00:14:15.166 --> 00:14:16.415
Is Maya beautiful?

139
00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.832
Very.

140
00:14:22.375 --> 00:14:24.040
This Maya must be doing something.

141
00:14:24.166 --> 00:14:26.374
She must be working, singing,
dancing...

142
00:14:26.458 --> 00:14:31.624
Maya dances, but not like you.
- What? - She dances only for herself.

143
00:14:36.083 --> 00:14:39.915
Excuse me, but she is a feeling,
A fantasy, she's beautiful...

144
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.915
...and she dances, and we've
got to find her in three months.

145
00:14:42.083 --> 00:14:43.165
So who is she?

146
00:14:43.583 --> 00:14:46.582
Maya is all these things,
and yet she is only Maya.

147
00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:49.999
Oh, Rahul. There you go
again on the same topic.

148
00:14:50.083 --> 00:14:53.290
I'm hungry. I'll get
something to eat. Okay?

149
00:14:53.375 --> 00:14:55.624
Hey, leave him alone.
- You all carry on. I'm coming.

150
00:15:29.041 --> 00:15:30.124
Maya.

151
00:15:37.041 --> 00:15:39.832
I've spent my life managing chores.
I'll make a decision today.

152
00:15:39.916 --> 00:15:42.624
Good morning, aunty!
- Silly girl! Where were you?

153
00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.999
I've been looking for you all over.
- I was outside.

154
00:15:45.208 --> 00:15:46.582
Now you must to come with me.

155
00:15:46.916 --> 00:15:49.665
Where? - I'm tired of
your uncle's daily nonsense.

156
00:15:49.833 --> 00:15:52.665
So, today there will be a fight,
and you must take my side.

157
00:15:52.916 --> 00:15:54.249
Okay. Let's go.

158
00:15:54.458 --> 00:15:59.999
"Sometimes, a thought..."

159
00:16:00.083 --> 00:16:05.540
"...crosses my mind..."

160
00:16:05.666 --> 00:16:06.999
Bravo, bravo!

161
00:16:07.083 --> 00:16:17.457
"As if you all have
been called only for me."

162
00:16:17.666 --> 00:16:27.874
Wow. - "You've been
scrubbing dishes so long..."

163
00:16:28.666 --> 00:16:37.499
"You've been made to sit in
the audience for my sake."

164
00:16:37.583 --> 00:16:40.332
Bravo, bravo. What a performance!

165
00:16:40.416 --> 00:16:43.874
Sir. Excuse me, Sir.

166
00:16:44.208 --> 00:16:46.582
Go on, Chandni... I mean, Shanti.

167
00:16:46.833 --> 00:16:49.624
If you permit, could
we have a tea break?

168
00:16:50.041 --> 00:16:52.999
Break whatever you want.

169
00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:56.999
If you don't mind, may I
have a word with your students?

170
00:16:57.208 --> 00:16:58.749
Of course.

171
00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:01.707
Watchman, gardener...
- Yes, ma'am.

172
00:17:01.833 --> 00:17:03.832
Shankar and Ramu.
- Yes.

173
00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:07.540
If you don't mind, will
you all get back to work now?

174
00:17:07.666 --> 00:17:10.624
Where are you going?
- Thank you.

175
00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:12.665
Why are you driving
away my audience? - Quiet.

176
00:17:13.416 --> 00:17:16.124
You gather all the servants
here and stall all the work.

177
00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:18.082
I have to do all the chores myself.

178
00:17:18.791 --> 00:17:20.874
Today onwards, no
more music recitals.

179
00:17:21.250 --> 00:17:24.082
Henceforth, only you will
listen to your music. No audience.

180
00:17:24.833 --> 00:17:29.207
My music isn't
appreciated in my own house.

181
00:17:29.291 --> 00:17:31.207
How would anybody
else appreciate it?

182
00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:35.957
Thanks to your aunt's attitude,
I could never become a great singer.

183
00:17:36.041 --> 00:17:39.874
I know, I know. Now forget
it and have a cup of tea.

184
00:17:39.958 --> 00:17:42.582
No, I don't want any tea.
- Oh come on, Uncle.

185
00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:46.124
Have a cup of tea,
and sing a song for me.

186
00:17:47.958 --> 00:17:50.040
Will you listen to my song?
- Of course.

187
00:17:50.291 --> 00:17:51.957
Really?
- Certainly.

188
00:17:52.041 --> 00:17:54.040
So let me have the tea.

189
00:17:54.125 --> 00:17:57.165
Pooja. There's a parcel for you.

190
00:17:58.458 --> 00:18:00.707
It's from Ajay!
Should be his cassette.

191
00:18:00.833 --> 00:18:02.540
I'll hear it right away.
- Hear my song first.

192
00:18:02.625 --> 00:18:03.790
Later, Uncle. please!

193
00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:07.040
See that? You always
drive my audience away

194
00:18:08.416 --> 00:18:10.040
What are you dreaming of?

195
00:18:12.291 --> 00:18:14.832
I was thinking how fast time flies.

196
00:18:15.791 --> 00:18:19.332
It seems like yesterday that Mr.
Khanna and Geeta had that accident...

197
00:18:20.083 --> 00:18:22.332
...and the ten-year
old Pooja came home.

198
00:18:22.916 --> 00:18:26.915
And now, it seems as if we
never had a life without her.

199
00:18:27.583 --> 00:18:30.165
And I have never seen such
close friends as Pooja and Ajay.

200
00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.832
'Hey, fatty! How are you?'

201
00:18:32.958 --> 00:18:34.540
Shut up, I'm not fat.

202
00:18:34.750 --> 00:18:37.082
'I've heard that these days
you've really put on some weight.'

203
00:18:37.333 --> 00:18:39.832
'Don't do that or no
one will marry you!'

204
00:18:39.958 --> 00:18:42.999
Idiot. Don't worry about my
marriage. Who's going to marry you?

205
00:18:43.083 --> 00:18:46.374
'By now, you must have finished
cursing me. So I'll proceed.'

206
00:18:46.625 --> 00:18:50.332
'I'm having fun, as usual, and
work and girls are keeping me busy.'

207
00:18:50.416 --> 00:18:53.290
'Tell you what? I never realised how
handsome I am when I was in India.'

208
00:18:54.625 --> 00:18:57.207
'Don't make faces. If you wish,
I can fax you...

209
00:18:57.291 --> 00:18:59.207
...a list of my girlfriends.'

210
00:18:59.291 --> 00:19:00.374
No, thank you.

211
00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:02.207
'For your information...
I've broken up with Tina...'

212
00:19:02.291 --> 00:19:04.249
'... because she
doesn't like Hindi films.'

213
00:19:04.375 --> 00:19:06.124
Thank God. She was so stupid.

214
00:19:06.208 --> 00:19:08.790
'And now I've fallen for
someone else.' - Who is she?

215
00:19:08.916 --> 00:19:12.124
'Don't yell, I'm telling you.
She's Dolly.' - Dolly?

216
00:19:12.208 --> 00:19:15.457
'There's no need to worry.
She loves Hindi movies.'

217
00:19:15.583 --> 00:19:17.999
Wow.
- 'Oh, I forgot.'

218
00:19:18.125 --> 00:19:20.124
'I might be coming to
Bombay for a few days.' - When?

219
00:19:20.666 --> 00:19:22.374
'No need to stand. Sit down.'

220
00:19:22.458 --> 00:19:25.540
'lt's not fixed as yet. As soon
as I get to know, I'll tell you.'

221
00:19:25.791 --> 00:19:27.207
'Okay, I'm off. Dolly
must be on her way...'

222
00:19:27.291 --> 00:19:29.665
'... and even though you haven't said
so, I'll convey your affections.'

223
00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:31.707
There's no need.
- 'Okay, I won't.'

224
00:19:31.875 --> 00:19:33.415
'Hey. Here she comes.
Okay, I'm going.'

225
00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:37.499
'Give mom and dad my love.
Take care, bye.'- Stupid.

226
00:19:43.333 --> 00:19:46.832
Hi. Nisha, where have you put
that cassette you took from my car?

227
00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:49.415
There was a really important
music piece of our play on it.

228
00:19:49.750 --> 00:19:52.624
Anything that goes into
your room vanishes forever.

229
00:19:53.083 --> 00:19:54.457
Where is the cassette?

230
00:19:54.791 --> 00:19:57.249
Rahul, don't you have the manners...

231
00:19:57.333 --> 00:20:00.082
...to knock before
coming into a girl's room.

232
00:20:00.166 --> 00:20:02.457
Is there a girl here?

233
00:20:02.583 --> 00:20:04.374
I... Stop it, Rahul. I'm serious.

234
00:20:04.458 --> 00:20:06.999
Look, don't give me all
this girl talk. Please!

235
00:20:07.083 --> 00:20:09.540
You have also entered my room at
times when I had nothing on. So?

236
00:20:09.916 --> 00:20:12.957
That's different. - Why is it
different? Don't I feel shy?

237
00:20:13.083 --> 00:20:14.415
Shut up, Rahul...
- You shut up!

238
00:20:15.291 --> 00:20:16.999
Go on now. Get my cassette.

239
00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.207
Oh. Thank...

240
00:20:20.541 --> 00:20:23.540
First say sorry, and then
you'll get the cassette.

241
00:20:24.125 --> 00:20:25.540
Must I say sorry?
- Yes.

242
00:20:25.708 --> 00:20:27.707
Say sorry to you?
- Yes.

243
00:20:28.333 --> 00:20:31.790
Why you... Nisha.
Nisha, give that here.

244
00:20:31.875 --> 00:20:33.290
Don't play stupid games with me.
- You stupid.

245
00:20:33.375 --> 00:20:36.290
If I catch you, you're dead.
- I'm not giving it to you.

246
00:20:36.458 --> 00:20:39.749
I'll get you. Give
me back my cassette.

247
00:20:39.875 --> 00:20:41.540
Come on, give me back my cassette.

248
00:20:42.625 --> 00:20:44.749
Give it to me.
- I won't!

249
00:20:44.833 --> 00:20:47.082
Give it to me, I say.
- Okay, okay.

250
00:20:47.458 --> 00:20:49.707
Now say you're sorry.
- Sorry for what?

251
00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:51.957
Sorry that you've wasted my time,
and made me run around.

252
00:20:52.083 --> 00:20:53.749
I'm not saying sorry.
- You won't?

253
00:20:54.208 --> 00:20:56.290
I'm sorry.
- Say you'll never annoy me again.

254
00:20:56.375 --> 00:20:58.207
I'll never annoy you.
- Say 'Rahul is the best'.

255
00:20:58.458 --> 00:20:59.540
Never!

256
00:21:00.166 --> 00:21:02.707
Rahul is the best. Okay?
- I know. Thank you very much.

257
00:21:04.166 --> 00:21:07.124
Rahul is the worst. Rahul
is a dog, Rahul is a monkey.

258
00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:09.999
Come what may, I'm not
going to dance in your play.

259
00:21:10.125 --> 00:21:12.415
So be it. I'll find
dancers like you aplenty.

260
00:21:12.541 --> 00:21:15.124
There isn't a single
dancer as good as me.

261
00:21:15.416 --> 00:21:22.999
"Fall in love."

262
00:21:23.125 --> 00:21:26.582
"Lose your heart to someone.
Fall in love..."

263
00:21:26.833 --> 00:21:30.249
"Fall in love..."

264
00:21:30.500 --> 00:21:33.707
"You're still young. Someone
out there is meant for you."

265
00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:37.749
"Find him, oh, lovelorn heart."

266
00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.082
Pooja!

267
00:21:39.166 --> 00:21:41.040
"You are young.
There's somebody for you."

268
00:21:41.166 --> 00:21:42.624
My wedding has been fixed.
- Wedding?

269
00:21:45.375 --> 00:21:47.832
I'm sorry.
- Six, seven, eight.

270
00:21:48.416 --> 00:21:53.374
"Fall in love..."

271
00:21:53.458 --> 00:21:54.749
What's wrong with you, Anjali?

272
00:21:55.416 --> 00:21:59.040
You're going to marry
someone you haven't chosen?

273
00:21:59.791 --> 00:22:01.415
Someone you hardly know.

274
00:22:01.541 --> 00:22:04.499
I do know him.
He's Mr. Kapoor's son.

275
00:22:04.625 --> 00:22:05.957
I've known him for years.

276
00:22:07.291 --> 00:22:08.749
But you don't love him.

277
00:22:09.625 --> 00:22:15.124
Well, Pooja. Love will
happen in due course.

278
00:22:16.458 --> 00:22:20.124
Love happens in due course?
Are you saying that, Anjali?

279
00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:22.207
We're not kids any more, Pooja.

280
00:22:23.416 --> 00:22:26.082
It's time we out grew
our world of fantasies.

281
00:22:27.041 --> 00:22:28.832
We are Indian girls.

282
00:22:29.875 --> 00:22:34.082
Our companion for life is never
same as the man in our dreams.

283
00:22:35.458 --> 00:22:39.582
We don't even choose him.
Someone else chooses him for us.

284
00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.124
We learn to love him.

285
00:22:43.833 --> 00:22:48.082
This is the truth, and the
sooner you realise it, the better.

286
00:22:49.166 --> 00:22:50.582
Don't make this mistake, Anjali.

287
00:22:52.208 --> 00:22:55.582
Someone, somewhere is made for you...

288
00:22:57.083 --> 00:22:58.790
...and you should wait for him.

289
00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:00.749
Perhaps he is the one.

290
00:23:02.333 --> 00:23:06.707
I believe that this is the
one who was made for me...

291
00:23:07.958 --> 00:23:10.290
...and I'm going to live
through with this belief.

292
00:23:11.375 --> 00:23:14.624
And who knows? This
might happen to you.

293
00:23:15.291 --> 00:23:21.082
Tomorrow you might marry a
man whom you merely know...

294
00:23:21.625 --> 00:23:26.999
...and slowly you might realise that
he was the one you were waiting for.

295
00:23:27.708 --> 00:23:30.790
"There's someone for you.
You find him out."

296
00:23:30.875 --> 00:23:32.124
Nothing like this is
going to happen to me.

297
00:23:32.875 --> 00:23:35.665
I'll choose my companion myself.

298
00:23:36.625 --> 00:23:39.999
This is impossible, Rahul.
There can't be a girl like this.

299
00:23:40.916 --> 00:23:43.915
What does that mean?
- It's a meaningless character.

300
00:23:44.291 --> 00:23:46.499
Maya refuses to come out
of her dreams.

301
00:23:46.583 --> 00:23:48.749
Modern girls aren't like this.

302
00:23:48.875 --> 00:23:50.707
What do you know?
You're not a even girl.

303
00:23:51.291 --> 00:23:52.874
Stop it, Rahul. I'm serious.

304
00:23:53.416 --> 00:23:55.749
Modern girls... - Maya is not
one of these modern girls.

305
00:23:55.833 --> 00:23:56.915
She's different.

306
00:23:58.541 --> 00:23:59.624
She is my Maya.

307
00:24:00.208 --> 00:24:03.957
Your Maya, indeed. What
do you know about girls?

308
00:24:04.041 --> 00:24:06.332
You know only one. And that's me!

309
00:24:06.416 --> 00:24:08.499
What do you mean? I don't
know anything about love...

310
00:24:08.583 --> 00:24:10.540
...and yet I make love stories.
What of it?

311
00:24:11.166 --> 00:24:13.957
Rahul, your Maya looks
absolutely crazy to me.

312
00:24:14.041 --> 00:24:16.790
Don't you call my Maya crazy.

313
00:24:16.958 --> 00:24:18.499
And you are the only
one who thinks like that.

314
00:24:18.583 --> 00:24:20.832
Nobody else talks like this.
- Definitely!

315
00:24:20.958 --> 00:24:23.582
Rahul, I think Nisha is right.
- Thank you.

316
00:24:23.666 --> 00:24:25.874
I don't understand 'Maya' either.

317
00:24:26.083 --> 00:24:28.749
Her character seems fake.
Isn't it Raju.

318
00:24:29.875 --> 00:24:30.957
I agree.

319
00:24:31.583 --> 00:24:33.540
Looking at it from a
psychological point of view...

320
00:24:33.625 --> 00:24:36.332
...I feel that you're on
your own trip of Utopia.

321
00:24:36.833 --> 00:24:38.540
I'm on a fantasy trip.

322
00:24:39.541 --> 00:24:42.374
I'm sorry, Maya is
not in. I'm sorry.

323
00:24:42.750 --> 00:24:46.540
You want to say something too?
- I think we need a lunch break.

324
00:24:46.666 --> 00:24:48.082
Exactly. See?

325
00:24:48.166 --> 00:24:51.749
I don't know if such a girl
exists or not... and I don't want to.

326
00:24:52.125 --> 00:24:55.457
Whether she is a lie, a
fantasy or crazy or whatever...

327
00:24:56.666 --> 00:24:57.749
...she's Maya.

328
00:24:58.625 --> 00:25:02.540
If you don't understand this,
I'm very sorry, I can't help it...

329
00:25:02.625 --> 00:25:04.915
...But all of you get
one thing straight.

330
00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:08.874
I am not going to change
Maya's character, come what may.

331
00:25:09.916 --> 00:25:10.999
Excuse me.

332
00:25:11.666 --> 00:25:14.582
What's this?
- I think Rahul's right.

333
00:25:14.666 --> 00:25:17.040
You shut up. You
are Rahul's yes-man.

334
00:25:17.166 --> 00:25:19.207
I was only saying that...
- Okay... what were you saying?

335
00:25:19.291 --> 00:25:21.040
Do you know of such a girl?
- No!

336
00:25:21.125 --> 00:25:22.749
Is your Soni like this?
- No.

337
00:25:22.916 --> 00:25:24.832
You figure the character of Maya?
- No.

338
00:25:24.958 --> 00:25:26.749
Should we do this play?
- Never.

339
00:25:27.083 --> 00:25:30.040
That's exactly what I've
been saying. - Right, but...

340
00:25:30.250 --> 00:25:31.415
Not again.
- Hey, what is going on?

341
00:25:31.500 --> 00:25:34.624
What do you think you are doing?
- Shut up.

342
00:25:41.750 --> 00:25:46.249
"That innocent face."

343
00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:49.040
"The mischief in her eyes."

344
00:25:49.541 --> 00:25:51.415
"Oh my!"

345
00:25:57.708 --> 00:26:00.624
"That innocent beauty,
with mischief in her eyes..."

346
00:26:00.708 --> 00:26:03.082
"...stands afar shying away."

347
00:26:04.541 --> 00:26:05.790
"Oh my!"

348
00:26:06.208 --> 00:26:11.249
"For a fleeting moment she
shows herself, and then turns away"

349
00:26:12.666 --> 00:26:14.040
"Oh my!"

350
00:26:14.333 --> 00:26:19.874
"If you look with my eyes, friend,
you can see her."

351
00:26:20.000 --> 00:26:22.624
"That innocent beauty,
with mischief in her eyes..."

352
00:26:22.708 --> 00:26:25.040
"...stands afar shying away."

353
00:26:25.125 --> 00:26:26.290
"Oh my!"

354
00:26:26.750 --> 00:26:31.790
"For a fleeting moment she
shows herself, and then turns away"

355
00:26:31.916 --> 00:26:33.332
"Oh my!"

356
00:26:33.583 --> 00:26:38.915
"If you look with my eyes, friend,
you can see her."

357
00:26:39.083 --> 00:26:43.457
"That innocent beauty,
with mischief in her eyes..."

358
00:26:44.166 --> 00:26:46.040
"Oh my!"

359
00:27:16.250 --> 00:27:21.457
"She's no ordinary girl,
she's a wonder."

360
00:27:21.541 --> 00:27:23.832
"How else can I describe her?"

361
00:27:25.541 --> 00:27:30.624
"Last night she came in my dreams
with her tresses flowing."

362
00:27:32.333 --> 00:27:37.290
"When I woke up, I wished
I could return to my dream."

363
00:27:37.791 --> 00:27:39.707
"If this is how I feel
without meeting her..."

364
00:27:39.791 --> 00:27:43.124
"...what would happen when I do?"

365
00:27:43.291 --> 00:27:45.707
"That innocent beauty,
with mischief in her eyes..."

366
00:27:45.791 --> 00:27:48.374
"...stands afar shying away"

367
00:27:49.708 --> 00:27:51.082
"Oh my!"

368
00:27:51.500 --> 00:27:56.665
"For a fleeting moment she shows
herself, and then turns away."

369
00:27:58.041 --> 00:27:59.290
"Oh my!"

370
00:27:59.666 --> 00:28:05.207
"If you look with my eyes, friend,
you can see her."

371
00:28:05.333 --> 00:28:09.665
"That innocent beauty,
with mischief in her eyes..."

372
00:28:10.333 --> 00:28:12.082
"Oh my!"

373
00:28:44.958 --> 00:28:52.582
"Dark as the monsoon clouds
is the kohl in her eyes"

374
00:28:54.291 --> 00:28:59.457
"Her gait has the grace
of the waves in the ocean"

375
00:29:01.250 --> 00:29:06.165
"Wonder what He created her of."

376
00:29:06.625 --> 00:29:11.999
"I wish she appears
before me out of nowhere."

377
00:29:12.208 --> 00:29:14.790
"That innocent beauty,
with mischief in her eyes..."

378
00:29:14.875 --> 00:29:17.165
"...stands afar shying away"

379
00:29:18.666 --> 00:29:19.832
"Oh my!"

380
00:29:20.333 --> 00:29:25.290
"For a fleeting moment she shows
herself, and then turns away."

381
00:29:26.875 --> 00:29:28.082
"Oh my!"

382
00:29:28.416 --> 00:29:33.957
"If you look with my eyes, friend,
you can see her"

383
00:29:34.083 --> 00:29:36.832
"That innocent beauty,
with mischief in her eyes..."

384
00:29:36.916 --> 00:29:38.957
"...stands afar shying away"

385
00:29:40.458 --> 00:29:43.457
"Oh my!"

386
00:29:43.541 --> 00:29:46.040
Yeah!
- Hey, what are you all doing?

387
00:29:48.916 --> 00:29:51.290
Rahul, how do you like this?
Hold this.

388
00:29:51.375 --> 00:29:54.499
Nisha, maybe you didn't notice
that everyone is staring at us.

389
00:29:55.000 --> 00:29:57.832
So what? I don't care.
- But I'm looking funny.

390
00:29:57.958 --> 00:30:00.707
Oh come on.
How do you like the orange?

391
00:30:00.791 --> 00:30:02.332
Very nice. Nisha.
- I'll be back in a moment.

392
00:30:02.416 --> 00:30:03.499
Nisha.

393
00:30:04.333 --> 00:30:05.874
'... you are requested to
collect your parcels...'

394
00:30:05.958 --> 00:30:07.707
'... from the delivery counters.'

395
00:30:08.875 --> 00:30:10.957
Shopping?
- Yes.

396
00:30:11.416 --> 00:30:12.999
Alone?
- Yes.

397
00:30:13.125 --> 00:30:17.499
Very good! Never make the mistake
of going shopping with a girl.

398
00:30:17.583 --> 00:30:20.499
How do you like this shirt?
Cool, isn't it? - You like it?

399
00:30:20.958 --> 00:30:23.124
I really like it.
- I love it! Let's go.

400
00:30:23.250 --> 00:30:26.415
Try it on once.
- Both of us like it... let's go.

401
00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:28.415
Rahul.
- To hell with Rahul!

402
00:30:29.625 --> 00:30:31.332
So sweet!
- What did you say?

403
00:30:31.458 --> 00:30:33.124
Nothing, nothing at all. Off you go!

404
00:30:37.291 --> 00:30:38.374
Who is it?

405
00:30:38.916 --> 00:30:40.915
Sorry! Idiot.

406
00:31:40.875 --> 00:31:42.040
Okay? Happy?

407
00:31:43.958 --> 00:31:45.499
Why are you laughing? What's up?

408
00:31:46.166 --> 00:31:47.624
Where are your jeans?

409
00:31:47.750 --> 00:31:49.332
I'm wearing it...

410
00:31:54.583 --> 00:31:55.665
It happens.

411
00:31:59.666 --> 00:32:00.749
Who is it?

412
00:32:24.041 --> 00:32:25.124
Crazy!

413
00:32:25.708 --> 00:32:34.915
Happy birthday to you.

414
00:32:35.416 --> 00:32:36.665
Happy birthday.

415
00:32:36.750 --> 00:32:41.790
Everybody clap... Open the cake box.
- Hey.

416
00:32:44.416 --> 00:32:47.499
Pooja. How did this happen?

417
00:32:47.791 --> 00:32:51.374
"What happened and
when did it happen?"

418
00:32:51.458 --> 00:32:54.207
How did this get swapped over?
I had ordered a chocolate cake.

419
00:32:55.166 --> 00:32:57.790
You must have picked up
someone else's parcel.

420
00:32:58.125 --> 00:33:00.707
I'm so stupid! I should've checked.

421
00:33:01.375 --> 00:33:04.040
I'm sorry, uncle.
- It's all right, dear.

422
00:33:04.166 --> 00:33:07.124
Other people celebrate their
birthdays by cutting a cake.

423
00:33:07.250 --> 00:33:09.874
I'll celebrate mine by
cutting sandwiches. No big deal.

424
00:33:09.958 --> 00:33:11.040
Come on. Come on.

425
00:33:11.125 --> 00:33:12.957
Let me see who got my cake.
- Where are the candles?

426
00:33:13.500 --> 00:33:15.165
Rahul.
- Pooja

427
00:33:16.541 --> 00:33:18.290
Who's Pooja?
- I don't know.

428
00:33:18.458 --> 00:33:20.624
And who's uncle?
- Must be Pooja's uncle.

429
00:33:21.166 --> 00:33:24.249
First time I sent you on an errand,
and you picked the wrong parcel.

430
00:33:24.375 --> 00:33:26.707
What have I done? I brought the
parcel the shopkeeper gave me.

431
00:33:26.833 --> 00:33:28.624
But you should have checked.

432
00:33:28.708 --> 00:33:30.665
Excuse me... but it
wasn't up to me to check.

433
00:33:30.750 --> 00:33:32.624
Next time, do it yourself. Okay?

434
00:33:32.750 --> 00:33:35.749
I'm hungry and this cake
looks awesome. Let's dig in.

435
00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:37.665
Stop it. No one's eating this cake.

436
00:33:37.750 --> 00:33:39.457
Why not? - Because it
belongs to someone else.

437
00:33:39.583 --> 00:33:41.082
They must be eating
our sandwiches too.

438
00:33:41.166 --> 00:33:44.832
There's an address written here.
It's nearby. Go and return it.

439
00:33:45.250 --> 00:33:46.332
Are you nuts?

440
00:33:46.916 --> 00:33:50.999
This is someone's birthday cake,
ordered with love.

441
00:33:51.166 --> 00:33:53.165
Someone's party will be ruined.
Go and give it back.

442
00:33:53.250 --> 00:33:54.332
I'm not going.

443
00:33:54.750 --> 00:33:56.332
Rahul
- To hell with Rahul!

444
00:33:56.583 --> 00:33:59.540
Jimmy, let's go and return it
and say 'Happy Birthday!' Come on.

445
00:33:59.625 --> 00:34:01.249
So sweet!
- What did you say?

446
00:34:01.666 --> 00:34:02.749
Nothing.

447
00:34:07.333 --> 00:34:08.415
Shut up!

448
00:34:08.958 --> 00:34:10.040
Yes?

449
00:34:10.875 --> 00:34:12.582
Good evening. Are you uncle?

450
00:34:12.833 --> 00:34:14.165
No, I'm aunty.

451
00:34:14.833 --> 00:34:18.374
Actually, by mistake I
got your cake, aunty.

452
00:34:18.500 --> 00:34:20.582
The sandwich man.
- That's right.

453
00:34:20.708 --> 00:34:23.957
Here's your cake, and
wishing you a happy birthday.

454
00:34:24.041 --> 00:34:25.874
Thank you and sorry.

455
00:34:26.291 --> 00:34:30.165
Why sorry? - Because we've
eaten all your sandwiches.

456
00:34:30.291 --> 00:34:34.790
That's all right. Actually, I ate
a bit of your cake on the way here.

457
00:34:35.583 --> 00:34:37.665
No wonder!
- Yes.

458
00:34:37.875 --> 00:34:40.957
Okay, I'll be off Uncle.
- No. Come in, and have some cake.

459
00:34:41.041 --> 00:34:42.957
No thanks. I'm in a hurry.
Some other time.

460
00:34:43.041 --> 00:34:45.832
Just a minute. Just
one minute, please.

461
00:34:46.000 --> 00:34:48.707
Let the person who
bought this cake thank you.

462
00:34:48.791 --> 00:34:49.915
There's no need.
- No, no!

463
00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:52.415
Uncle.
- Pooja, Pooja.

464
00:34:52.833 --> 00:34:55.165
Pooja, Pooja.
- Yes, Uncle.

465
00:34:55.250 --> 00:34:58.165
That poor man, whose
sandwiches you picked up by mistake...

466
00:34:58.250 --> 00:35:00.915
...has brought the cake back.
- How sweet!

467
00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:02.624
He's at the door. Go and thank him.
- Okay.

468
00:35:02.708 --> 00:35:04.415
Thank him.
- Okay.

469
00:35:04.541 --> 00:35:09.165
"The cake has brought
a twinkle in my eyes..."

470
00:35:09.250 --> 00:35:13.957
"...and a musical rhythm to
the strings of my stomach."

471
00:35:14.083 --> 00:35:17.082
"The cake is here."

472
00:35:22.208 --> 00:35:24.415
To fit or not to fit. Not to fit.

473
00:35:25.166 --> 00:35:26.249
What a fool!

474
00:35:49.416 --> 00:35:51.124
'We welcome you.'

475
00:35:51.250 --> 00:35:52.832
'Happy Valentines Day.'

476
00:35:55.125 --> 00:35:58.582
Why are you buying all this stuff?

477
00:35:58.916 --> 00:36:01.207
Come on, Anjali. It's
Valentine's Day today.

478
00:36:01.541 --> 00:36:02.665
Valentine's day?

479
00:36:03.125 --> 00:36:06.915
What is this Valentine's day?
- Don't you know?

480
00:36:07.250 --> 00:36:10.665
The one you love most in the
world is called your Valentine.

481
00:36:11.166 --> 00:36:14.499
On this day, all lovers pour
