728
00:56:32.875 --> 00:56:34.665
The sun is up, Pooja.

729
00:56:36.125 --> 00:56:37.207
Pooja.

730
00:56:51.208 --> 00:56:52.624
What is it? What is it?

731
00:56:53.958 --> 00:56:57.582
You? You idiot. Is this
the way to wake someone up?

732
00:56:57.916 --> 00:57:01.707
I'm so sorry, but seeing you fast
asleep, I just couldn't resist it.

733
00:57:01.916 --> 00:57:04.040
How could I miss out
on such an opportunity?

734
00:57:04.125 --> 00:57:07.415
You idiot. Stupid.
- I'm sorry... sorry, sorry

735
00:57:07.583 --> 00:57:11.582
Listen, get ready quickly.
We've got to go to the airport.

736
00:57:11.833 --> 00:57:13.749
Airport? Are you going somewhere?

737
00:57:14.250 --> 00:57:17.290
No. We are.

738
00:57:17.750 --> 00:57:19.082
We? And where are we going?

739
00:57:19.583 --> 00:57:21.165
Well, that's a surprise.

740
00:57:21.666 --> 00:57:24.332
It's not far from India,
it's nearby.

741
00:57:24.583 --> 00:57:26.874
We'll return by tonight's flight.
Get ready quickly.

742
00:57:27.916 --> 00:57:29.999
I don't get you.

743
00:57:30.083 --> 00:57:33.582
Silly. It's very simple.
I have to go on some business.

744
00:57:33.666 --> 00:57:35.540
It'll take me just an hour...
just sign some papers...

745
00:57:35.583 --> 00:57:37.457
...and then I am free.

746
00:57:37.791 --> 00:57:39.540
If you come along,
you'll see a new city...

747
00:57:39.625 --> 00:57:42.082
...as well as get some shopping done.

748
00:57:42.166 --> 00:57:43.999
And anyway I'm leaving
for London tomorrow.

749
00:57:44.250 --> 00:57:45.540
That leaves only today...

750
00:57:45.625 --> 00:57:48.207
...which I want to
spend with you. So simple.

751
00:57:48.291 --> 00:57:51.207
But Ajay, I must find out if
it's okay with uncle and aunt.

752
00:57:51.291 --> 00:57:55.082
I've already got their approval.
It's only you who has to decide.

753
00:57:55.166 --> 00:57:58.624
So fatty, are you coming or not?

754
00:57:58.708 --> 00:58:00.249
Of course, I'm coming!
- That's great.

755
00:58:00.333 --> 00:58:01.707
Then hurry up and get ready.
The flight is on time.

756
00:58:01.791 --> 00:58:04.624
Wait a minute.
What's that under your eye?

757
00:58:04.708 --> 00:58:05.790
Where?
- There.

758
00:58:06.958 --> 00:58:09.332
Now wait, you fatty!
Stop there, fatty!

759
00:58:10.291 --> 00:58:12.540
Never mind. I'll get you for this.
- Come and get me.

760
00:58:13.541 --> 00:58:16.207
Oh!

761
00:58:16.958 --> 00:58:20.415
You're going shopping,
aren't you? We'll see.

762
00:58:41.583 --> 00:58:50.415
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

763
00:58:55.083 --> 00:58:58.582
"It makes lovers meet
for the first time..."

764
00:58:58.666 --> 00:59:02.999
"...and it ignites
passion in their hearts."

765
00:59:03.833 --> 00:59:07.540
"It shows them the path of love."

766
00:59:08.041 --> 00:59:11.915
"It brings joys and tears as well."

767
00:59:12.000 --> 00:59:21.124
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

768
00:59:21.208 --> 00:59:24.999
"It brings along sleepless nights."

769
00:59:25.458 --> 00:59:29.040
"It steals sleep and solace."

770
00:59:29.833 --> 00:59:33.540
"It gives you real
and unreal dreams."

771
00:59:33.958 --> 00:59:37.790
"It brings joys and tears as well."

772
00:59:37.875 --> 00:59:46.832
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

773
01:00:22.125 --> 01:00:25.124
"Those who follow the heart..."

774
01:00:26.458 --> 01:00:29.957
"...become crazy as well."

775
01:00:30.791 --> 01:00:34.707
"The eternal traveler
finds his destination..."

776
01:00:34.791 --> 01:00:38.457
"...but loses track of the
paths that led him there."

777
01:00:38.541 --> 01:00:47.457
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

778
01:00:56.791 --> 01:00:59.915
"I wouldn't recognise him by face..."

779
01:01:01.125 --> 01:01:04.290
"...nor would I know him by name."

780
01:01:05.458 --> 01:01:09.749
"I wouldn't think twice..."

781
01:01:09.833 --> 01:01:13.165
"...before I
blindly follow my heart."

782
01:01:13.333 --> 01:01:22.290
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

783
01:02:14.625 --> 01:02:18.790
"We all heed the heart..."

784
01:02:18.875 --> 01:02:23.290
"...but the heart heeds no one."

785
01:02:23.541 --> 01:02:31.165
"The world knows I lost
myself to him but he doesn't."

786
01:02:31.250 --> 01:02:40.249
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

787
01:02:49.250 --> 01:02:52.624
"So be the tales of love,
if they would."

788
01:02:53.750 --> 01:02:57.040
"Those indexing insanity."

789
01:02:58.041 --> 01:03:01.832
"All the troubles plaguing
the face of this earth..."

790
01:03:01.916 --> 01:03:05.499
"...are the graces of
this unreasonable heart."

791
01:03:05.583 --> 01:03:14.790
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

792
01:03:14.958 --> 01:03:18.957
"It brings along sleepless nights."

793
01:03:19.458 --> 01:03:23.082
"It steals sleep and solace."

794
01:03:23.708 --> 01:03:27.499
"It gives you real
and unreal dreams."

795
01:03:27.958 --> 01:03:31.790
"It brings joys and tears as well."

796
01:03:31.958 --> 01:03:33.624
"The heart is crazy...

797
01:03:34.125 --> 01:03:35.790
"...the heart is besotted."

798
01:03:36.041 --> 01:03:38.374
"The heart is crazy..."

799
01:03:38.458 --> 01:03:40.957
"...the heart is besotted."

800
01:04:13.750 --> 01:04:15.957
'Passengers travelling
on Air India's flight...'

801
01:04:16.041 --> 01:04:17.124
'... Al101 are requested to
see the immigration office...'

802
01:04:17.208 --> 01:04:19.749
Well, Mister Ajay. Time to go.

803
01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:22.165
Now I'll have to go.
- Did you say something?

804
01:04:25.250 --> 01:04:26.832
Pooja, I want to tell you something.

805
01:04:27.333 --> 01:04:28.957
Tell me. What is it?

806
01:04:29.833 --> 01:04:35.249
This quick business trip of a
couple of days was all a pretence.

807
01:04:36.750 --> 01:04:38.457
I came here for something else.

808
01:04:41.208 --> 01:04:43.082
It's been eight
years since I left India.

809
01:04:44.250 --> 01:04:46.207
I've earned enough
of respect and money.

810
01:04:46.375 --> 01:04:47.540
I've had enough of this hectic life.

811
01:04:48.166 --> 01:04:51.082
I want to stop now.
I want to settle down now.

812
01:04:53.708 --> 01:04:54.957
And whenever I close my eyes...

813
01:04:55.041 --> 01:05:00.957
...to think whom I'd like to
spend the rest of my life with...

814
01:05:01.041 --> 01:05:03.207
...it is always your face that I see.

815
01:05:05.458 --> 01:05:08.957
In those moments we spent together,
I don't know how or when...

816
01:05:09.041 --> 01:05:12.290
...my feelings for you
turned to love.

817
01:05:15.666 --> 01:05:18.499
But I had no clue
about your feelings.

818
01:05:19.875 --> 01:05:22.999
I don't know whether
you like someone...

819
01:05:23.083 --> 01:05:26.082
...or whether there is
anyone in your life.

820
01:05:26.541 --> 01:05:28.499
That's what I came here to find out.

821
01:05:28.625 --> 01:05:31.124
I don't know what you think of me.

822
01:05:32.083 --> 01:05:36.540
I don't even know if you would want
to spend your whole life with me.

823
01:05:37.666 --> 01:05:40.999
But I know for sure
that I love you...

824
01:05:41.083 --> 01:05:43.832
...and I want to marry you.

825
01:05:48.666 --> 01:05:51.582
'This is the last and final
call for passengers travelling...'

826
01:05:51.666 --> 01:05:54.665
'... on Air India's
flight Al 101 to London.'

827
01:05:54.750 --> 01:05:56.249
I'll go towards the
departure gate now.

828
01:05:57.833 --> 01:06:00.499
Once I'm there,
I'll turn around and look.

829
01:06:02.791 --> 01:06:06.374
If your answer is affirmative,
stay here.

830
01:06:08.416 --> 01:06:11.624
And if you're not here,
I'll understand.

831
01:06:14.041 --> 01:06:16.415
And one more thing.

832
01:06:17.833 --> 01:06:20.040
Don't forget that
whatever your decision is...

833
01:06:20.125 --> 01:06:25.040
...we were friends, we are friends,
and we'll always be friends. Okay?

834
01:06:41.083 --> 01:06:44.082
'Who knows, it may
happen to you too.'

835
01:06:44.375 --> 01:06:47.082
'You might end up marrying a man...'

836
01:06:47.166 --> 01:06:50.165
'... you only know but don't love.'

837
01:06:50.666 --> 01:06:54.082
'... and then gradually you
realise that he's the one...'

838
01:06:54.166 --> 01:06:56.290
'... whom you've been waiting for.'

839
01:07:24.333 --> 01:07:27.207
What? But why did you stay?

840
01:07:28.541 --> 01:07:32.124
Sometimes, there's so much joy
in making someone else happy...

841
01:07:32.208 --> 01:07:33.915
...that I can't
think of anything else.

842
01:07:34.625 --> 01:07:38.040
You should have seen his face, Anjali.
He was so happy.

843
01:07:38.833 --> 01:07:40.790
I have never seen him so happy.

844
01:07:41.333 --> 01:07:42.415
And what about your happiness?

845
01:07:43.583 --> 01:07:45.707
You don't love him, Pooja.

846
01:07:46.375 --> 01:07:47.457
Love?

847
01:07:48.750 --> 01:07:53.499
What about love?
It happens in due course. Isn't it?

848
01:07:55.166 --> 01:07:57.582
And we are Indian girls.

849
01:07:58.708 --> 01:08:00.749
We can't choose our life partners.

850
01:08:02.166 --> 01:08:03.665
Someone else chooses
our life partners for us.

851
01:08:05.250 --> 01:08:08.415
We learn to love them.

852
01:08:09.583 --> 01:08:10.665
Isn't that true?

853
01:08:11.333 --> 01:08:14.165
The girl finally outgrows her
dreams and turns to a woman.

854
01:08:15.208 --> 01:08:18.165
No, Anjali. The girl
has become a woman...

855
01:08:18.250 --> 01:08:21.999
...but she hasn't
given up her dreams.

856
01:08:23.708 --> 01:08:25.790
She believes in them completely,
even now.

857
01:08:27.625 --> 01:08:33.082
She's sure that Ajay is the one
for whom she has always been waiting.

858
01:08:34.750 --> 01:08:38.332
Maybe He is delaying the indication.

859
01:08:39.625 --> 01:08:42.207
I'm sure that you'll
be very happy with Ajay.

860
01:08:43.250 --> 01:08:44.332
I hope so.

861
01:09:04.250 --> 01:09:06.582
What happened, Nisha?
Take her to the doctor, hurry.

862
01:09:07.125 --> 01:09:11.332
Slow down, Rahul.
We're almost there. Slow down.

863
01:09:13.125 --> 01:09:14.207
Get a stretcher, Suppandi.

864
01:09:14.791 --> 01:09:17.040
Admit her.
- Take this. - Okay, sir.

865
01:09:18.958 --> 01:09:21.415
Hi, Doctor.
- There's no need to worry.

866
01:09:21.833 --> 01:09:24.457
It's a small fracture.
She'll go home in a week or so.

867
01:09:24.625 --> 01:09:27.249
I told you Nisha would
start dancing again in a week.

868
01:09:27.333 --> 01:09:31.374
I'm talking about
going home, not dancing.

869
01:09:32.041 --> 01:09:33.457
She can't dance for
another three months.

870
01:09:34.166 --> 01:09:35.624
Three months?
- Yes, Rahul.

871
01:09:36.333 --> 01:09:37.540
Her heel is very delicate.

872
01:09:38.250 --> 01:09:41.499
If she doesn't take care,
the fracture could recur...

873
01:09:42.250 --> 01:09:44.124
...and it could be more serious.

874
01:09:44.958 --> 01:09:47.749
Does she know this.
- Yes. - May I see her?

875
01:09:48.041 --> 01:09:50.624
Of course. You don't need my
permission. - Thank you, Doctor.

876
01:09:50.750 --> 01:09:51.832
I'll see you guys.

877
01:09:52.500 --> 01:09:54.832
Who's going to get me a cup of tea?

878
01:09:57.458 --> 01:10:00.249
God! You'll never
learn to knock, will you?

879
01:10:00.333 --> 01:10:01.707
Don't give me that girl talk.

880
01:10:01.833 --> 01:10:03.707
I have something very
important to discuss.

881
01:10:06.083 --> 01:10:08.707
Yes, tell me. - Can you see
me properly? How many fingers?

882
01:10:09.208 --> 01:10:10.582
Stop it, Rahul.
- Jokes apart.

883
01:10:10.916 --> 01:10:14.624
Okay! Look, this Dr. Kapoor
of yours isn't up to much.

884
01:10:15.083 --> 01:10:18.499
I think you should see
some other doctor. - Why?

885
01:10:18.583 --> 01:10:20.415
This doctor was talking about
getting you discharged in a week.

886
01:10:21.125 --> 01:10:22.957
So what?
- No, it's not done.

887
01:10:23.291 --> 01:10:25.415
It's been such a task
getting you to the hospital.

888
01:10:25.708 --> 01:10:27.624
You should spend at least
a month or two in here.

889
01:10:27.916 --> 01:10:31.707
Mean... - And while you are away,
we'll also have some peace.

890
01:10:31.791 --> 01:10:34.124
Rahul, I hate you.
You're so horrible. - Slowly...

891
01:10:34.208 --> 01:10:36.457
You're always making fun of me.
I hate you. You're so bad.

892
01:10:37.000 --> 01:10:38.374
Nisha, behave yourself.
Sorry, nurse.

893
01:10:38.458 --> 01:10:39.624
She has gone mad with the pain.

894
01:10:39.708 --> 01:10:41.749
But don't worry, I'll take
care of her. I'm a psychologist.

895
01:10:41.875 --> 01:10:42.957
Sis...
- Rahul.

896
01:10:43.208 --> 01:10:44.915
Yes?
- I'm sorry.

897
01:10:45.791 --> 01:10:46.874
For what?

898
01:10:48.041 --> 01:10:50.249
I've put you
through so much trouble.

899
01:10:51.416 --> 01:10:54.332
You've taken so much
money from the sponsors...

900
01:10:54.416 --> 01:10:57.332
...and how would you
find a dancer so soon?

901
01:10:58.500 --> 01:11:00.332
And for three months, I...
- Now look...

902
01:11:00.625 --> 01:11:03.540
...there's no need for you to worry.

903
01:11:04.083 --> 01:11:05.249
Rahul.
- Rahul's done for!

904
01:11:05.333 --> 01:11:06.874
What do you think?
You're a good dancer?

905
01:11:07.458 --> 01:11:09.832
There are scores of
fabulous dancers in town.

906
01:11:10.000 --> 01:11:13.332
Sure, but you'll never find...
- A dancer like you, right?

907
01:11:13.416 --> 01:11:16.790
Right.
- Now you don't worry about this.

908
01:11:16.916 --> 01:11:19.957
Now get some rest and
I'll see you in the evening.

909
01:11:20.041 --> 01:11:22.790
Okay. - And you don't need to
eat the boring hospital food.

910
01:11:22.875 --> 01:11:25.624
I'll bring some food.
We'll eat together.

911
01:11:26.041 --> 01:11:27.207
It's a deal. Right?

912
01:11:27.958 --> 01:11:29.290
Bye.
- Bye.

913
01:11:31.791 --> 01:11:34.165
Rahul.
- I know. Chinese, right?

914
01:11:34.416 --> 01:11:35.499
Right.

915
01:11:38.708 --> 01:11:41.249
Not to worry. It'll all work out.
- How will it all work out?

916
01:11:41.875 --> 01:11:42.957
We've borrowed money
from the sponsors,

917
01:11:43.041 --> 01:11:44.124
...and paid a
deposit for the stadium.

918
01:11:44.291 --> 01:11:46.415
Where are we going to
find a dancer like Nisha?

919
01:11:46.833 --> 01:11:49.874
Come on, if we try, don't you
think we can find one good dancer?

920
01:11:50.125 --> 01:11:51.957
There are plenty of dance schools.

921
01:11:52.083 --> 01:11:53.874
One is right next to
our rehearsal hall.

922
01:11:54.166 --> 01:11:55.874
We'll find a dancer there tomorrow.

923
01:11:55.958 --> 01:11:57.915
Yes! Yes, Jimmy. You're right.

924
01:11:58.375 --> 01:12:00.874
How about that, Rahul?
Come on, relax.

925
01:12:01.125 --> 01:12:02.665
Whatever happens
will be for the best.

926
01:12:03.000 --> 01:12:04.707
Let's go, and have
some chilled beer.

927
01:12:05.000 --> 01:12:06.999
No... You go ahead. I'm not
in the mood. - Come on, buddy!

928
01:12:07.500 --> 01:12:10.499
Relax, pal. Try to understand.
He's tired.

929
01:12:10.750 --> 01:12:12.165
Come on, we'll push off.
- See you guys. Take care.

930
01:12:12.500 --> 01:12:14.874
Bye, bye.
- Come on, Supandi. - I'll see you.?

931
01:12:14.958 --> 01:12:16.624
First you give me your
address and phone number.

932
01:12:17.875 --> 01:12:18.957
Maya...

933
01:12:21.416 --> 01:12:22.499
I'll find her.

934
01:16:03.750 --> 01:16:04.832
Maya.

935
01:16:41.250 --> 01:16:43.499
"Water, water."

936
01:16:43.750 --> 01:16:48.124
"Water, water in my eyes."
- Excuse me...

937
01:16:48.208 --> 01:16:49.832
The sandwich man.

938
01:16:50.166 --> 01:16:53.040
Shanti, has a parcel
come here by mistake? - No...

939
01:16:53.125 --> 01:16:56.124
I haven't come for a parcel today.
- Then tell me what I can do for you.

940
01:16:56.208 --> 01:16:59.665
I want to meet your daughter.
- I don't have a daughter.

941
01:17:00.125 --> 01:17:01.207
No daughter?
- No.

942
01:17:01.291 --> 01:17:03.457
Then sir, Ms. Pooja Malhotra?

943
01:17:04.041 --> 01:17:06.707
Pooja is like my daughter.
- I see.

944
01:17:06.833 --> 01:17:08.832
But how do you know her?

945
01:17:09.333 --> 01:17:11.957
I saw her last night.
- Night?

946
01:17:13.541 --> 01:17:15.749
Where?
- In the dancing school.

947
01:17:16.041 --> 01:17:17.832
She dances really well.
- So?

948
01:17:18.708 --> 01:17:20.332
So, I wanted to meet her.
- What for?

949
01:17:21.333 --> 01:17:23.207
I wanted to ask her something.
- What did you want to ask her?

950
01:17:23.791 --> 01:17:26.707
If she'd... sort of... with me...
- What with you?

951
01:17:27.166 --> 01:17:31.165
If she'd work with me.
- What work?

952
01:17:31.583 --> 01:17:35.165
I do plays, and I'm looking for
a dancer - You are doing a play.

953
01:17:35.875 --> 01:17:36.957
Yes.

954
01:17:37.125 --> 01:17:40.082
Are you a director?
- Yes. I'm sorry.

955
01:17:40.250 --> 01:17:43.124
I'm sorry. Why
didn't you tell me before?

956
01:17:43.208 --> 01:17:46.582
I did, when you asked me.
- I'm sorry. Come on in.

957
01:17:47.083 --> 01:17:49.249
Actually, I'm a singer.
- I see.

958
01:17:49.333 --> 01:17:52.499
I've done years of practice. Sit...

959
01:17:53.000 --> 01:17:55.082
As it happens with
many great artistes...

960
01:17:55.166 --> 01:17:58.624
...you don't really meet
too many connoisseurs.

961
01:17:58.791 --> 01:18:03.165
You've met me today. You
don't know how lucky you are.

962
01:18:03.291 --> 01:18:05.707
I know, sir but I've
come to meet Pooja.

963
01:18:05.791 --> 01:18:08.665
Now that you have met me,
you'll meet Pooja, too.

964
01:18:08.791 --> 01:18:10.624
I won't give you a
penny more than 75.

965
01:18:10.708 --> 01:18:14.040
The prices have gone up, ma'am.
Rs.80, no less.

966
01:18:14.458 --> 01:18:15.540
Only last week I bought it at...

967
01:18:15.625 --> 01:18:17.957
...that price and the prices
have shot up within a week?

968
01:18:18.041 --> 01:18:20.165
Trust me, ma'am.
That's the correct price.

969
01:18:20.291 --> 01:18:22.124
You can taste for
yourself how sweet it is.

970
01:18:22.208 --> 01:18:24.957
I will give you Rs.75 and no more.
- Seventy five...

971
01:18:25.041 --> 01:18:27.415
Show me the watermelon.
- Here you are, sir. - Show...

972
01:18:31.708 --> 01:18:33.624
Seventy-five is the right price.
How many do you want, Ma'am?

973
01:18:34.166 --> 01:18:35.832
Just one.
- Pack this for Ma'am.

974
01:18:35.916 --> 01:18:38.040
But...
- Oh, come on!

975
01:18:38.291 --> 01:18:40.457
It's your first sale in the day,
and you're haggling for five bucks?

976
01:18:41.125 --> 01:18:43.207
Come on, give it
to ma'am. I'm there.

977
01:18:46.916 --> 01:18:49.165
Hi.
- Hi.

978
01:18:50.166 --> 01:18:51.249
Recognise me?

979
01:18:51.416 --> 01:18:53.707
We met last night at
your dancing school.

980
01:18:54.250 --> 01:18:55.707
Remember?
- Oh, yes.

981
01:18:56.500 --> 01:18:58.790
I'm Rahul. You must've heard of me?

982
01:18:59.916 --> 01:19:00.957
No.

983
01:19:01.041 --> 01:19:05.790
Well, never mind. Actually
you are a pretty good dancer.

984
01:19:06.666 --> 01:19:07.749
Thank you.

985
01:19:08.166 --> 01:19:11.165
Actually, I'm doing
some musical shows...

986
01:19:11.250 --> 01:19:14.457
...and I need a special
dancer for a special role.

987
01:19:15.166 --> 01:19:16.249
When I saw you dancing yesterday...

988
01:19:16.333 --> 01:19:20.457
...I thought that
you'd be ideal for this.

989
01:19:22.083 --> 01:19:25.124
So what do you think?
Would you be interested?

990
01:19:26.750 --> 01:19:27.832
No, thanks.

991
01:19:29.208 --> 01:19:30.249
Rahul is done for.

992
01:19:30.375 --> 01:19:31.457
Sir, watermelon!

993
01:19:31.541 --> 01:19:33.249
My career's at stake here and all
you can think of is that watermelon.

994
01:19:33.333 --> 01:19:34.415
Here, take this. Watermelon.

995
01:19:36.458 --> 01:19:38.665
Excuse me, but perhaps
you misunderstand me.

996
01:19:38.750 --> 01:19:41.415
The shows I'm talking
about are no ordinary shows.

997
01:19:41.583 --> 01:19:42.665
Here I am.

998
01:19:42.750 --> 01:19:46.207
They're high-class shows with
a very high-class audience...

999
01:19:46.291 --> 01:19:48.207
...and I am sure you
would also enjoy doing it.

1000
01:19:48.416 --> 01:19:49.915
Why don't you give it a try?

1001
01:19:50.333 --> 01:19:52.207
Not for me, for the sake of art.

1002
01:19:52.916 --> 01:19:56.040
Dancing is my hobby.
- That's really good.

1003
01:19:56.291 --> 01:19:59.582
But dancing on stage in front
of an audience makes me nervous.

1004
01:19:59.708 --> 01:20:01.999
What's there to be nervous?
- I don't think I can do it.

1005
01:20:02.083 --> 01:20:05.415
No, no.
- I'm sorry... - No problem. Just...

1006
01:20:07.375 --> 01:20:08.457
Take 3.

1007
01:20:10.833 --> 01:20:12.457
Excuse me. I'm sorry.

1008
01:20:12.708 --> 01:20:14.540
Look, I'm in a tight spot.

1009
01:20:14.791 --> 01:20:16.790
Actually, my lead dancer
has fractured her foot.

1010
01:20:16.958 --> 01:20:18.332
I've already
borrowed money for the show.

1011
01:20:18.583 --> 01:20:21.499
If we don't perform, I'll not only
incur a loss but also lose face.

1012
01:20:21.625 --> 01:20:25.332
Just come once for a rehearsal,
and if you don't like it, it's fine.

1013
01:20:25.416 --> 01:20:27.999
But please, just once.
Please come to the rehearsal.

1014
01:20:28.083 --> 01:20:31.290
I'm really very sorry.
- Please - I can't do it.

1015
01:20:31.375 --> 01:20:34.082
Please.
- Why don't you hire someone else?

1016
01:20:34.916 --> 01:20:36.249
I beg of you, please.
- What are you doing?

1017
01:20:36.333 --> 01:20:38.665
You don't know me.
I'm a stubborn and crazy guy.

1018
01:20:38.916 --> 01:20:40.665
I'm not budging until you agree.
- Look. Please get up.

1019
01:20:40.750 --> 01:20:41.832
Please come just
once to a rehearsal.

1020
01:20:41.916 --> 01:20:42.999
Don't come back if you don't want to.
- Everyone's looking at us.

1021
01:20:43.083 --> 01:20:44.415
Please. Please come, just once!

1022
01:20:44.500 --> 01:20:46.749
Okay. I'll come. - You will?
Promise? - Promise.

1023
01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:48.415
When?
- Tomorrow. - What time?

1024
01:20:48.583 --> 01:20:50.040
2:00pm.
- Can't you come at one?

1025
01:20:50.125 --> 01:20:53.582
Okay, I'll come at one. - Thank you
very much. Thank you for all this.

1026
01:20:55.000 --> 01:20:56.082
By the way, I hope you know that...

1027
01:20:56.166 --> 01:20:57.707
...our rehearsal hall is right
next to your dancing school.

1028
01:20:57.833 --> 01:20:59.874
I know. - We're neighbours,
you know?! - I know.

1029
01:21:00.166 --> 01:21:02.332
Thank you very much. Thank you.
Thank you very much.

1030
01:21:05.250 --> 01:21:06.332
Ma'am.

1031
01:21:06.833 --> 01:21:08.040
You'll come, won't you?

1032
01:21:10.375 --> 01:21:11.540
Yes, you will.

1033
01:21:13.708 --> 01:21:14.790
Ma'am.

1034
01:21:16.375 --> 01:21:17.457
Yes.

1035
01:21:19.291 --> 01:21:21.082
For you. Yes.

1036
01:21:25.541 --> 01:21:26.665
He's crazy.

1037
01:21:29.791 --> 01:21:32.582
How is this sketch?
- No that good. This one's better.

1038
01:21:32.666 --> 01:21:33.749
Sir.

1039
01:21:33.833 --> 01:21:36.582
That's okay. But this one, this is
what I don't like. Make this proper.

1040
01:21:36.791 --> 01:21:37.874
I'll do that.

1041
01:21:37.958 --> 01:21:40.499
The colour scheme's okay. Okay.

1042
01:21:40.583 --> 01:21:41.665
But look at this one,
here, this one...

1043
01:21:42.958 --> 01:21:45.915
Rahul, you said that
girl would come at 1:00pm...

1044
01:21:46.250 --> 01:21:48.540
It's already 4:00pm.
I don't think she'll come.

1045
01:21:48.750 --> 01:21:49.832
So what should I do?

1046
01:21:50.166 --> 01:21:51.707
So if she doesn't come,
won't we do our play?

1047
01:21:52.083 --> 01:21:54.082
I was only...
- Go and get on with your own thing.

1048
01:21:54.416 --> 01:21:56.124
Go.
- Okay, relax.

1049
01:21:58.958 --> 01:22:02.957
What happened?
- Please, don't disturb me.

1050
01:22:06.333 --> 01:22:07.832
Quiet, quiet everybody.

1051
01:22:11.333 --> 01:22:13.624
Ballu, spotlight on the entrance.

1052
01:22:34.000 --> 01:22:35.707
Hi.
- Hi.

1053
01:22:37.375 --> 01:22:40.124
Rahul. You must've heard of me?

1054
01:22:59.541 --> 01:23:01.624
Cut it. No, no.

1055
01:23:03.625 --> 01:23:04.874
No, Pooja. No.

1056
01:23:05.875 --> 01:23:06.957
No, Pooja.

1057
01:23:07.500 --> 01:23:09.749
You're not putting
your heart into it.

1058
01:23:10.125 --> 01:23:13.332
You are concentrating
more on the steps and music.

1059
01:23:14.750 --> 01:23:18.499
I don't want to see
how well you dance.

1060
01:23:18.583 --> 01:23:20.332
I have already seen that,
and you are very good.

1061
01:23:21.083 --> 01:23:24.665
I want to see whether
you are Maya or not.

1062
01:23:25.875 --> 01:23:29.207
I want to see the zenith
of Maya's love and passion.

1063
01:23:30.500 --> 01:23:34.624
I want to see what happens
when Maya pours her heart out.

1064
01:23:35.708 --> 01:23:36.790
Right?

1065
01:23:37.416 --> 01:23:39.499
Okay. We'll try it once more.

1066
01:23:43.416 --> 01:23:44.790
All right, music.

1067
01:23:59.583 --> 01:24:00.665
Cut it!

1068
01:24:00.750 --> 01:24:02.332
Why don't you understand
what I'm trying to tell you?

1069
01:24:03.458 --> 01:24:04.582
Forget that there's
anyone sitting here.

1070
01:24:05.083 --> 01:24:06.207
Forget that there's music playing.

1071
01:24:06.583 --> 01:24:09.124
Forget that this is a rehearsal.
Just think of Maya.

1072
01:24:09.375 --> 01:24:10.665
God knows where you're lost.

1073
01:24:10.875 --> 01:24:13.540
I've cried myself hoarse that
I don't want to see your dance.

1074
01:24:13.750 --> 01:24:16.165
I don't want to see you dance.
I want to see your madness!

1075
01:24:16.375 --> 01:24:18.207
Maya's madness...

1076
01:24:22.166 --> 01:24:24.124
I'm sorry, Pooja.
- Don't touch me.

1077
01:24:26.125 --> 01:24:28.665
I'm really sorry, Pooja.
I was just...

1078
01:24:28.750 --> 01:24:30.832
Never in my life has
anyone yelled at me like that.

1079
01:24:31.083 --> 01:24:33.624
I know, Pooja. I'm an idiot.

1080
01:24:33.875 --> 01:24:35.832
I don't know how to talk to girls.

1081
01:24:35.958 --> 01:24:38.207
I told you I can't do it.

1082
01:24:38.375 --> 01:24:39.915
But you're doing it really well.

1083
01:24:40.500 --> 01:24:42.249
It's just that I'm
going on about Maya.

1084
01:24:42.333 --> 01:24:44.332
I don't understand this Maya.
- Never mind...

1085
01:24:44.416 --> 01:24:46.832
I don't want to do this.
- Don't worry if you don't understand.

1086
01:24:47.166 --> 01:24:50.540
We don't have to do this today.
We can do it tomorrow. Okay?

1087
01:24:50.750 --> 01:24:53.582
I don't want to do it tomorrow either.
I'm not doing this. - Okay.

1088
01:24:53.791 --> 01:24:55.999
Maya, relax.
- My name is Pooja.

1089
01:24:56.875 --> 01:24:58.415
Of course, it's Pooja.

1090
01:24:59.750 --> 01:25:02.540
I'm sorry. Sit down, please. Sit

1091
01:25:02.916 --> 01:25:06.499
I'm really sorry, Pooja.
Don't dance if you don't want to...

1092
01:25:06.583 --> 01:25:07.665
...but please stop crying.

1093
01:25:08.125 --> 01:25:09.207
Don't want water? No problem.

1094
01:25:09.333 --> 01:25:12.124
You see Pooja, it's a habit
with me to yell during rehearsals.

1095
01:25:12.583 --> 01:25:14.332
I wasn't having a go at you.

1096
01:25:15.458 --> 01:25:19.624
I was only trying to explain
to you about Maya that's all.

1097
01:25:20.833 --> 01:25:24.707
Pooja, maybe you just
don't understand Maya.

1098
01:25:27.166 --> 01:25:29.499
Maya is the kind of girl...

1099
01:25:29.583 --> 01:25:34.290
...who lives in a dream world.

1100
01:25:35.791 --> 01:25:40.540
She believes that one day
her dream prince will come...

1101
01:25:40.625 --> 01:25:42.290
...and carry her away.

1102
01:25:43.541 --> 01:25:46.540
Her friends have
always made fun of her...

1103
01:25:46.625 --> 01:25:48.290
...but that did not shake her belief.

1104
01:25:50.333 --> 01:25:54.540
And today, she has met
the man of her dreams...

1105
01:25:54.625 --> 01:25:57.457
...and she's dancing.

1106
01:25:58.875 --> 01:26:00.540
There is love in her dance...

1107
01:26:01.541 --> 01:26:03.624
There's mad passion and arrogance.

1108
01:26:04.750 --> 01:26:11.582
As if to say,
"I knew he would come..."

1109
01:26:11.666 --> 01:26:18.499
"...and now, see, he has come."
"My dream man has come."

1110
01:26:46.916 --> 01:26:47.999
Music.

1111
01:27:22.166 --> 01:27:28.249
Wow, wonderful. - Brilliant.
- Brilliant. - Thank you.

1112
01:27:35.041 --> 01:27:36.165
It was nice.

1113
01:27:36.416 --> 01:27:38.457
Brilliant. Absolutely brilliant.

1114
01:27:38.666 --> 01:27:42.374
Nisha, I can't believe we got
such a good girl so quickly!

1115
01:27:42.708 --> 01:27:45.665
Had I not got the
right girl for this role...

1116
01:27:45.750 --> 01:27:46.832
...l'd have cancelled the play...

1117
01:27:46.916 --> 01:27:50.124
...given back the money, and
willingly faced the music.

1118
01:27:51.166 --> 01:27:53.249
But I was destined to meet Pooja.

1119
01:27:55.208 --> 01:27:57.332
Her name is Pooja?
- No, it's Jeetendra.

1120
01:27:57.666 --> 01:27:58.749
Of course it's Pooja.

1121
01:28:01.291 --> 01:28:04.290
Is she beautiful?
- Really beautiful.

1122
01:28:04.750 --> 01:28:07.957
Remember how I described Maya?
She's just like her.

1123
01:28:08.791 --> 01:28:13.457
That innocent face, those
dreamy eyes and that bashfulness.

1124
01:28:15.291 --> 01:28:17.332
She is too good, Nisha.
She's brilliant.

1125
01:28:17.750 --> 01:28:18.832
Yes.

1126
01:28:20.041 --> 01:28:21.290
Is she a good dancer?

1127
01:28:21.583 --> 01:28:24.249
When she dances, you can't
take your eyes off her.

1128
01:28:24.375 --> 01:28:26.957
I know that you will go
crazy when you see her.

1129
01:28:27.166 --> 01:28:28.290
I see.
- Yes.

1130
01:28:28.750 --> 01:28:31.082
But can she act?

1131
01:28:31.208 --> 01:28:34.957
But of course, she can.
If she can't act, what am I for?

1132
01:28:35.166 --> 01:28:38.499
If I can get you to act,
I can get anyone to act.

1133
01:28:38.791 --> 01:28:39.874
Very funny.

1134
01:28:41.000 --> 01:28:43.457
There's no water, no soft drink
and you've called me for dinner.

1135
01:28:43.791 --> 01:28:45.999
Wait a minute, and I'll
get something to drink.

1136
01:28:49.208 --> 01:28:50.290
Rahul.

1137
01:28:52.125 --> 01:28:53.624
Is she as good a dancer as me?

1138
01:28:54.333 --> 01:28:57.915
Are you crazy? There's
no dancer as good as you.

1139
01:28:58.375 --> 01:29:00.124
Right.
- Right.

1140
01:29:05.916 --> 01:29:06.999
Idiot.

1141
01:29:08.000 --> 01:29:09.540
Can't even lie properly.

1142
01:30:48.000 --> 01:30:50.540
There go your pants.

1143
01:30:57.000 --> 01:30:58.165
The stitches gave away.

1144
01:31:07.541 --> 01:31:09.499
Hey Shruti, get my bag.
- Relax.

1145
01:31:09.583 --> 01:31:14.499
Let's go! - Okay, we'll push
off now. See you tomorrow...

1146
01:31:14.583 --> 01:31:16.749
Bye...
- See you tomorrow.

1147
01:31:30.291 --> 01:31:31.499
May I say something, Pooja?
- What?

1148
01:31:32.791 --> 01:31:36.457
When you smile...
- I know, I look good.

1149
01:31:38.083 --> 01:31:39.165
Then?

1150
01:31:39.375 --> 01:31:42.374
When you laugh, it rains.

1151
01:31:43.958 --> 01:31:45.040
Give it back.

1152
01:31:51.875 --> 01:31:55.540
"With the gait of a horse,
with the majesty of an elephant."

1153
01:31:56.250 --> 01:31:59.915
"Oh, king of the rains,
where do you come from?"

1154
01:32:00.666 --> 01:32:04.332
"With the gait of a horse,
with the majesty of an elephant."

1155
01:32:05.083 --> 01:32:08.749
"Oh, king of the rains,
where do you come from?"

1156
01:32:31.458 --> 01:32:35.832
"I know a girl, when she smiles..."

1157
01:32:40.333 --> 01:32:57.165
"I know a girl, when she smiles,
the rains come pouring down."

1158
01:32:57.958 --> 01:33:02.457
"I know a boy, when he sings..."

1159
01:33:06.458 --> 01:33:23.540
"I know a boy, when he sings,
the rain clouds mask the sky."

1160
01:33:55.375 --> 01:33:59.290
"The clouds have descended..."

1161
01:33:59.708 --> 01:34:03.707
"They stand in our path."

1162
01:34:04.333 --> 01:34:08.165
"Tell us what your
intentions are, oh clouds."

1163
01:34:08.666 --> 01:34:11.999
"Won't you let us go home?"

1164
01:34:12.708 --> 01:34:16.582
"There's rain ahead,
a storm behind."

1165
01:34:17.125 --> 01:34:20.707
"The weather is treacherous.
Oh, where can we go?"

1166
01:34:26.041 --> 01:34:33.957
"I know a girl, when she smiles,
the rains come pouring down."

1167
01:34:34.791 --> 01:34:42.749
"I know a boy, when he sings,
the rain clouds mask the sky."

1168
01:35:23.416 --> 01:35:27.290
"The heavy sky
stoops low with clouds."

1169
01:35:27.708 --> 01:35:31.499
"Everything has
come to a standstill."

1170
01:35:32.250 --> 01:35:36.374
"How lovely is this season."

1171
01:35:36.541 --> 01:35:39.915
"Take the sign of the rains."

1172
01:35:40.750 --> 01:35:44.374
"In such a weather, say something..."

1173
01:35:45.083 --> 01:35:48.790
"...do something.
Why do you stand silent?"

1174
01:35:56.208 --> 01:35:59.832
"With the gait of a horse,
with the majesty of an elephant."

1175
01:36:00.583 --> 01:36:04.207
"Oh king of the rains,
where do you come from?"

1176
01:36:04.958 --> 01:36:08.624
"With the gait of a horse,
with the majesty of an elephant."

1177
01:36:09.333 --> 01:36:12.915
"Oh king of the rains,
where do you come from?"

1178
01:36:40.250 --> 01:36:48.207
"I know a girl, when she smiles,
the rains come pouring down."

1179
01:36:48.958 --> 01:36:57.040
"I know a boy, when he sings,
the rain clouds mask the sky."

1180
01:37:46.208 --> 01:37:49.957
The doctor has said clearly that
you can't go out of the house.

1181
01:37:50.291 --> 01:37:52.874
There's no need for you to
strain yourself trying to get up.

1182
01:37:53.333 --> 01:37:55.624
Now get into your bed, and rest.

1183
01:37:57.416 --> 01:37:59.582
Who are you calling now?

1184
01:37:59.791 --> 01:38:02.249
Rahul.
- Oh yes, he called...

1185
01:38:02.333 --> 01:38:06.124
...to say that he's at Soni's house.

1186
01:38:06.416 --> 01:38:10.082
At Soni's? Oh yes, Soni and
Jimmy are getting engaged today.

1187
01:38:10.333 --> 01:38:13.665
Aunt, get my clothes out quickly.
I want to go there. I'll just come.

1188
01:38:13.791 --> 01:38:16.040
Look, I'll call the doctor.
- Aunt, please!

1189
01:38:16.333 --> 01:38:17.540
She just won't listen.

1190
01:38:19.250 --> 01:38:23.249
"The girl is beautiful..."

1191
01:38:23.333 --> 01:38:27.374
"The boy looks morose..."

1192
01:38:27.500 --> 01:38:29.707
"The two don't match..."

1193
01:38:31.708 --> 01:38:37.749
"The two don't match..."
"They don't make a good pair..."

1194
01:38:37.833 --> 01:38:39.415
I'll not give this to you.

1195
01:38:41.250 --> 01:38:42.374
I hate these weddings.

1196
01:38:43.083 --> 01:38:45.040
I don't understand
why people get married.

1197
01:38:45.458 --> 01:38:49.290
If two people have decided to
spend their whole lives together...

1198
01:38:49.375 --> 01:38:52.124
...why are the others
making such a fuss?

1199
01:38:52.291 --> 01:38:53.374
Why are they all getting excited?

1200
01:38:53.875 --> 01:38:54.957
These days it has become a fashion...

1201
01:38:55.041 --> 01:38:58.082
...to have seven days
long wedding celebrations.

1202
01:38:58.375 --> 01:38:59.457
Give me a break.

1203
01:38:59.875 --> 01:39:02.332
Get married, have a quiet ceremony,
and then go home and sleep.

1204
01:39:02.791 --> 01:39:05.207
I've even come to hate
the word 'marriage'.

1205
01:39:05.375 --> 01:39:07.124
Excuse me, may I have another one?

1206
01:39:07.541 --> 01:39:10.290
But the one good thing
is that in all this fuss...

1207
01:39:10.375 --> 01:39:11.665
...you get lots of goodies to eat.

1208
01:39:11.958 --> 01:39:13.040
Thank you. Have you eaten?

1209
01:39:13.333 --> 01:39:14.415
Later.
- Let's sit.

1210
01:39:14.875 --> 01:39:16.207
I really love weddings.

1211
01:39:17.125 --> 01:39:20.332
The small rituals, dancing,
singing, and making merry...

1212
01:39:20.416 --> 01:39:22.999
...I love every bit of it.
- Very good.

1213
01:39:24.333 --> 01:39:25.957
I'm going to have all
of them at my wedding.

1214
01:39:27.708 --> 01:39:28.790
Are you getting married?

1215
01:39:31.916 --> 01:39:32.957
Yes.

1216
01:39:37.500 --> 01:39:38.915
I mean, you never mentioned it.

1217
01:39:40.958 --> 01:39:42.040
When are you going to do it?

1218
01:39:42.708 --> 01:39:44.540
Actually, nothing is fixed yet.

1219
01:39:45.458 --> 01:39:46.957
He works abroad.

1220
01:39:47.666 --> 01:39:48.749
When he comes back...

1221
01:39:48.833 --> 01:39:52.290
...we'll fix a date when
we've found an auspicious time.

1222
01:39:53.166 --> 01:39:55.124
That's why I haven't
mentioned this to anyone.

1223
01:39:56.041 --> 01:39:58.207
I see. Congratulations.

1224
01:39:59.708 --> 01:40:00.790
Thanks.

1225
01:40:05.000 --> 01:40:07.957
Rahul, when are you
getting married to Nisha?

1226
01:40:09.416 --> 01:40:11.040
Nisha and me? Are you crazy?

1227
01:40:11.708 --> 01:40:13.207
The two of us are just good friends.

1228
01:40:13.500 --> 01:40:15.374
There's no chance of us
ever getting married...

1229
01:40:15.458 --> 01:40:17.624
...and in any case,
marriage and me, no thank you.

1230
01:40:18.291 --> 01:40:21.457
Actually, I don't believe at all
in the institution of marriage.

1231
01:40:22.208 --> 01:40:23.374
I don't know how two people decide...

1232
01:40:23.458 --> 01:40:25.832
...to spend their whole
life with each other.

1233
01:40:26.041 --> 01:40:28.415
I fail to understand
and I'm certain...

1234
01:40:28.500 --> 01:40:33.540
...there can't be a girl who
could spend her whole life with me!

1235
01:40:34.125 --> 01:40:36.707
You're mistaken.
There is one such girl.

1236
01:40:37.125 --> 01:40:40.457
Where is she?
- Somewhere or the other.

1237
01:40:42.500 --> 01:40:43.582
Rubbish.

1238
01:40:45.500 --> 01:40:49.874
I've always believed that God
made all relationships of the heart.

1239
01:40:51.000 --> 01:40:52.540
But then He left it to
us to find each other.

1240
01:40:54.041 --> 01:40:55.790
He created all of us in pairs.

1241
01:40:56.583 --> 01:40:59.040
For every one of us
there is a soul-mate.

1242
01:40:59.958 --> 01:41:02.124
You just have to
wait till you meet her.

1243
01:41:03.833 --> 01:41:06.332
Do you think that's true?

1244
01:41:06.541 --> 01:41:08.290
At least in my life,
that's the ultimate truth.

1245
01:41:10.500 --> 01:41:11.582
True.

1246
01:41:14.500 --> 01:41:17.790
That means that you've
found your soul mate.

1247
01:41:19.750 --> 01:41:21.165
Yes. I've found him.

1248
01:41:22.083 --> 01:41:24.040
I found my soul mate.

1249
01:41:31.791 --> 01:41:33.499
Something is amiss.
- What?

1250
01:41:35.291 --> 01:41:37.999
The dessert is amazing.
Have some. - No.

1251
01:41:38.791 --> 01:41:39.874
Okay.

1252
01:41:45.541 --> 01:41:46.624
I don't know where he keeps it...

1253
01:41:46.708 --> 01:41:49.915
...Nisha! When were you discharged
from the hospital? - Hey, Ballu.

1254
01:41:50.125 --> 01:41:51.707
I ran away from hospital.
- Great.

1255
01:41:52.000 --> 01:41:53.957
Jimmy and Soni will be
delighted to see you.

1256
01:41:54.041 --> 01:41:56.249
Where are they? - They are sitting
in the lawn, go and meet them.

1257
01:41:56.500 --> 01:42:00.540
Rahul is there, isn't he?
- Rahul's gone to drop Pooja home.

1258
01:42:00.625 --> 01:42:02.249
Ballu.
- Coming. You go ahead.

1259
01:42:03.166 --> 01:42:06.749
"He has come, he has
come with a sword..."

1260
01:42:06.833 --> 01:42:07.915
Pooja.

1261
01:42:13.708 --> 01:42:15.499
Thanks. See you tomorrow.

1262
01:42:15.583 --> 01:42:17.082
Pooja.
- What?

1263
01:42:19.125 --> 01:42:21.624
It's that story you
told me at Soni's.

1264
01:42:22.666 --> 01:42:25.415
That some special girl
is made for me... etc, etc...

1265
01:42:26.208 --> 01:42:27.332
I've been thinking about that.

1266
01:42:29.083 --> 01:42:31.832
I don't get something.
- What?

1267
01:42:33.541 --> 01:42:37.249
How would I know who's made for me?

1268
01:42:37.750 --> 01:42:39.415
You have so much
faith in this theory.

1269
01:42:39.916 --> 01:42:42.415
I'm sure you know how I'm
going to meet this girl.

1270
01:42:42.916 --> 01:42:47.457
I mean, will she be holding
a placard with my name on it?

1271
01:42:47.958 --> 01:42:49.540
Or, when I see her would
there be a clap of thunder...

1272
01:42:49.625 --> 01:42:51.540
...and a bolt of lightning?

1273
01:42:51.625 --> 01:42:52.915
Would music start playing?
What would happen?

1274
01:42:54.833 --> 01:42:55.915
He will tell you.

1275
01:42:56.875 --> 01:42:58.249
He will give just one sign...

1276
01:42:58.750 --> 01:43:00.957
...and your heart
would recognise the girl.

1277
01:47:19.541 --> 01:47:21.999
I've tried reasoning with her...
but she just wouldn't listen.

1278
01:47:22.666 --> 01:47:24.332
She does what she wants.
- Hi, Doctor.

1279
01:47:24.500 --> 01:47:26.874
Doctor.
- Rahul, good you came.

1280
01:47:27.291 --> 01:47:29.832
I'm fed up with this girl.
- Why? What happened?

1281
01:47:30.166 --> 01:47:34.124
I told her clearly that she
needs to stay at home to rest.

1282
01:47:34.541 --> 01:47:37.707
But look at her, she's
packing her bags to go somewhere.

1283
01:47:38.125 --> 01:47:40.290
Where to?
- How would I know?

1284
01:47:40.791 --> 01:47:43.457
I've tried my best to explain.
- She doesn't listen to me.

1285
01:47:43.541 --> 01:47:45.707
You're the only one
who could convince her.

1286
01:47:45.875 --> 01:47:48.207
Don't worry, she won't go anywhere.

1287
01:47:48.291 --> 01:47:49.665
I'll go in and take
her to task right away.

1288
01:47:49.750 --> 01:47:51.957
Okay? - Best of luck.
- Okay, see you. - Bye

1289
01:47:54.000 --> 01:47:55.082
Nisha.

1290
01:47:57.958 --> 01:48:00.457
What are you doing, Nisha?
Are you nuts?

1291
01:48:00.791 --> 01:48:02.165
The doctor told you to rest, right?

1292
01:48:02.541 --> 01:48:04.207
By the way, where are you off to?

1293
01:48:04.583 --> 01:48:06.582
I'm going to London.
- London?

1294
01:48:07.041 --> 01:48:08.832
Well, Mum and Dad
keep calling me...

1295
01:48:08.916 --> 01:48:11.499
...and it's been months
since I met them.

1296
01:48:12.666 --> 01:48:13.832
I thought I'd visit them.

1297
01:48:14.166 --> 01:48:16.832
Besides, I want to
run away from here.

1298
01:48:17.458 --> 01:48:19.040
Want to run away? From whom?

1299
01:48:21.000 --> 01:48:23.499
From myself.
- What's all this nonsense, Nisha?

1300
01:48:25.375 --> 01:48:27.124
I've begun to get
scared of myself, Rahul.

1301
01:48:29.833 --> 01:48:31.207
I want to leave...

1302
01:48:32.833 --> 01:48:34.499
...so that I can avoid doing
things like the one I did yesterday.

1303
01:48:34.583 --> 01:48:37.040
Nisha, you haven't done
anything of the sort.

1304
01:48:37.250 --> 01:48:38.499
You were just dancing.

1305
01:48:38.583 --> 01:48:39.999
Look here...
- Rahul...

1306
01:48:40.958 --> 01:48:44.082
...now we should stop
evading the truth.

1307
01:48:45.333 --> 01:48:48.457
We both know what the problem is.

1308
01:48:50.000 --> 01:48:51.082
What's the problem?

1309
01:48:53.666 --> 01:48:54.832
The problem is that...

1310
01:48:54.916 --> 01:49:00.457
...I love you, and you don't love me.

1311
01:49:05.541 --> 01:49:08.874
Look here, Nisha...
- I know...

1312
01:49:08.958 --> 01:49:13.040
...that you know how much I love you.

1313
01:49:14.750 --> 01:49:15.915
That night I wasn't sozzled enough...

1314
01:49:16.000 --> 01:49:19.624
...to not hear what
my heart was saying.

1315
01:49:21.250 --> 01:49:25.874
Actually, Rahul, we've
become such good friends...

1316
01:49:25.958 --> 01:49:29.790
...that we take each
other for granted.

1317
01:49:31.083 --> 01:49:36.832
So I think that a bit of space
will give us time to think.

1318
01:49:39.000 --> 01:49:40.915
But I'm sure...

1319
01:49:41.000 --> 01:49:45.957
...that when I'm not here,
you'll miss me a lot.

1320
01:49:46.916 --> 01:49:49.124
Then maybe then
you'd realise my worth.

1321
01:49:49.916 --> 01:49:53.915
One thing is certain,
that an idiot like you...

1322
01:49:54.000 --> 01:49:56.290
...doesn't deserve a girl like me.

1323
01:49:57.666 --> 01:50:00.915
And I don't know why,
but I feel that...

1324
01:50:01.000 --> 01:50:02.915
...when I come back...

1325
01:50:03.000 --> 01:50:09.707
...you'll be on your knees
begging me to get married to you.

1326
01:50:10.708 --> 01:50:12.874
And who knows, at that point in time
I may not be in the mood for it.

1327
01:50:14.250 --> 01:50:15.332
Get lost.

1328
01:50:15.708 --> 01:50:16.874
Well, maybe you
haven't seen your face...

1329
01:50:17.291 --> 01:50:18.332
It's better than yours.

1330
01:50:19.666 --> 01:50:25.082
Hey, Nisha...
- Rahul.

1331
01:50:32.166 --> 01:50:35.707
Nisha, you're really nice.

1332
01:50:37.125 --> 01:50:38.790
I know. Come on now...

1333
01:50:38.875 --> 01:50:40.790
I must meet everyone on
my way to the airport.

1334
01:50:41.416 --> 01:50:42.665
Come on, Rahul, hurry up.

1335
01:50:49.958 --> 01:50:51.707
We'll see you.
- Bye, see you guys.

1336
01:50:51.791 --> 01:50:53.790
Take care...
- I'll really miss you. - Thanks.

1337
01:50:54.083 --> 01:50:56.290
Bye.
- Enjoy yourself.

1338
01:50:56.541 --> 01:50:59.290
Take care.
- Bye, Nisha. - Bye buddy.

1339
01:50:59.375 --> 01:51:00.999
Rahul, has our stuff arrived?

1340
01:51:01.083 --> 01:51:05.290
Ballu is mad.

1341
01:51:07.000 --> 01:51:08.999
We haven't been properly introduced.

1342
01:51:09.666 --> 01:51:11.665
Let's start from the beginning.

1343
01:51:12.166 --> 01:51:14.207
Hi! I'm Nisha.
- I'm Pooja.

1344
01:51:15.375 --> 01:51:16.999
Now that we are friends...

1345
01:51:17.083 --> 01:51:21.999
...will you forgive me
for what I did yesterday?

1346
01:51:22.333 --> 01:51:24.415
Forgive you? For what?

1347
01:51:24.916 --> 01:51:29.207
Pooja, what I did with you
yesterday, wasn't right.

1348
01:51:30.291 --> 01:51:32.999
Actually, ever since
this place was built...

1349
01:51:33.083 --> 01:51:36.207
...l'm the only one
who's danced on this floor.

1350
01:51:37.291 --> 01:51:39.290
This floor has become my identity.

1351
01:51:40.041 --> 01:51:46.374
So when I heard that someone else
had taken my place... I felt bad.

1352
01:51:47.375 --> 01:51:50.332
Without seeing you or
knowing you, I was jealous.

1353
01:51:51.708 --> 01:51:53.374
I shouldn't have felt that way.

1354
01:51:54.208 --> 01:51:56.957
Had I been in your place,
I'd have done the same.

1355
01:51:57.708 --> 01:52:00.707
Moreover, I really
enjoyed dancing with you.

1356
01:52:01.666 --> 01:52:03.249
You were the one dancing.

1357
01:52:04.458 --> 01:52:05.957
I was doing something else.

1358
01:52:07.625 --> 01:52:09.665
I'm really sorry, Pooja.
- It's okay

1359
01:52:09.750 --> 01:52:11.749
Come on, Nisha. The pilot of
your flight just called for you.

1360
01:52:12.416 --> 01:52:16.790
I always told Rahul that there could
never be another dancer like me.

1361
01:52:17.416 --> 01:52:18.499
But I can't say that any more.

1362
01:52:19.708 --> 01:52:20.790
And I'm sure that...

1363
01:52:20.875 --> 01:52:24.124
...no one can play the role
of Maya better than you.

1364
01:52:24.583 --> 01:52:26.790
Not even me. All the best...

1365
01:52:26.875 --> 01:52:28.124
Bye. See you.
- Thank you! Bye.

1366
01:52:28.375 --> 01:52:29.457
Come.

1367
01:52:29.541 --> 01:52:33.165
Who is coming to drop
me to the airport? - Me!

1368
01:53:26.375 --> 01:53:27.957
Hi. I'm Rahul.

1369
01:53:28.708 --> 01:53:29.790
You must have heard of me?

1370
01:53:30.500 --> 01:53:32.374
I'm looking for a special
dancer for a special role.

1371
01:53:32.875 --> 01:53:37.415
I saw you dance yesterday and
felt you would be ideal for this.

1372
01:53:39.625 --> 01:53:41.415
Check, check... 69...

1373
01:53:41.625 --> 01:53:44.040
Ballu, what are you doing?
Throw the spotlight properly.

1374
01:53:45.291 --> 01:53:48.790
Pooja, good, good. But...

1375
01:53:50.291 --> 01:53:53.415
I think that you are not opening up.

1376
01:53:54.125 --> 01:53:57.249
I want to see how Maya
looks when she's happy.

1377
01:53:57.708 --> 01:54:01.749
I want to see the zenith of
Maya's passion and love. Okay?

1378
01:54:02.583 --> 01:54:04.457
Do it again. Okay.

1379
01:54:05.500 --> 01:54:08.082
Quiet everybody.
Take it from the top.

1380
01:54:09.166 --> 01:54:10.249
Music!

1381
01:54:11.166 --> 01:54:12.415
Cut it! Cut it!

1382
01:54:12.708 --> 01:54:14.165
Haven't I told you to
forget that you are you...

1383
01:54:14.250 --> 01:54:16.207
...to forget that there
are people sitting here?

1384
01:54:16.291 --> 01:54:17.374
Forget that there's a
rehearsal going on here.

1385
01:54:17.583 --> 01:54:18.665
But you refuse to understand.

1386
01:54:18.916 --> 01:54:19.999
Pack up.

1387
01:54:22.916 --> 01:54:24.832
I don't get one thing, Pooja.

1388
01:54:25.916 --> 01:54:28.415
How I would know which
girl was made for me?

1389
01:54:29.333 --> 01:54:31.874
Will she be holding a
placard with my name on it?

1390
01:54:31.958 --> 01:54:34.207
When I see her, would
there be a clap of thunder...

1391
01:54:34.291 --> 01:54:35.415
...and a flash of lightning?

1392
01:56:22.583 --> 01:56:28.499
"Oh dear, what's happening?
I don't really know."

1393
01:56:29.041 --> 01:56:35.332
"I only hope this does not
turn into a tale of love."

1394
01:56:35.458 --> 01:56:41.290
"Oh dear, what's going on?
Nobody really knows."

1395
01:56:41.916 --> 01:56:47.957
"But if this is a tale
of love, then so be it."

1396
01:57:36.708 --> 01:57:41.790
"Take my hand in yours,
as long as you are here."

1397
01:57:43.125 --> 01:57:48.374
"Let's sit talking,
as long as we can."

1398
01:57:49.458 --> 01:57:53.374
"Let's look into
each other's eyes..."

1399
01:57:53.458 --> 01:57:55.665
"...as long as the night lasts."

1400
01:57:56.041 --> 01:58:02.874
"Oh dear, what's going on?
Nobody really knows."

1401
01:58:08.833 --> 01:58:14.124
"How do I describe
the state of my heart?"

1402
01:58:15.375 --> 01:58:20.749
"Even the dewdrops seem to burn,
with the fever of my heart."

1403
01:58:21.791 --> 01:58:28.082
"Why do I feel as if
someone has caressed me"

1404
01:58:28.166 --> 01:58:31.249
"Oh dear, what's going on?"

1405
01:58:31.500 --> 01:58:34.249
"I don't really know."

1406
01:58:34.625 --> 01:58:40.624
"I only hope this does not
turn into a tale of love."

1407
01:58:41.166 --> 01:58:43.832
"Oh dear, what's going on?"

1408
01:58:44.166 --> 01:58:47.499
"Nobody really knows."

1409
01:58:47.583 --> 01:58:50.415
"But if this is a tale of love..."

1410
01:58:50.500 --> 01:58:53.707
"...then so be it."

1411
01:59:23.041 --> 01:59:28.415
"Please move away for a while,
so I can collect my feelings..."

1412
01:59:29.333 --> 01:59:34.665
"...and calm the
violent beating of my heart."

1413
01:59:35.833 --> 01:59:42.124
"Let's slow down so that we
don't move ahead of time."

1414
01:59:42.208 --> 01:59:48.624
"Oh dear, what's happening?
Nobody really knows."

1415
01:59:55.166 --> 02:00:00.332
"There is something
between us, don't deny it."

1416
02:00:01.583 --> 02:00:06.999
"And no one know
how far it would go."

1417
02:00:08.083 --> 02:00:14.249
"For you should know, your
heart is not what it was."

1418
02:00:14.500 --> 02:00:17.499
"Oh dear, what's going on?"

1419
02:00:17.666 --> 02:00:20.874
"I don't really know."

1420
02:00:20.958 --> 02:00:23.832
"I only hope..."

1421
02:00:23.916 --> 02:00:27.207
"...this does not turn
into a tale of love."

1422
02:00:27.375 --> 02:00:30.165
"Oh dear, what's going on?"

1423
02:00:30.541 --> 02:00:33.207
"I don't really know"

1424
02:00:33.833 --> 02:00:36.749
"I only hope this does not..."

1425
02:00:36.833 --> 02:00:39.957
"...turn into a tale of love."

1426
02:01:09.541 --> 02:01:12.207
I hope your uncle would be asleep
so I won't have to hear him sing.

1427
02:01:15.666 --> 02:01:16.832
Bye.
- Bye

1428
02:01:19.458 --> 02:01:21.957
Rahul, I forgot to tell you...
- What?

1429
02:01:22.125 --> 02:01:24.499
I can't attend rehearsal tomorrow.
- Why?

1430
02:01:25.000 --> 02:01:27.499
Tomorrow I'm going to Khandala.
- Khandala? Why?

1431
02:01:27.791 --> 02:01:30.249
My sister lives there.
- Which sister?

1432
02:01:30.916 --> 02:01:32.165
She's my dance teacher.

1433
02:01:32.791 --> 02:01:35.582
She taught me everything I know.

1434
02:01:36.000 --> 02:01:37.332
It's her birthday tomorrow.

1435
02:01:38.416 --> 02:01:41.040
If I say no, will you not go?

1436
02:01:42.791 --> 02:01:47.499
I'd go anyway, but if you
said yes, I'd go happily.

1437
02:01:49.625 --> 02:01:52.540
I'm joking. Go on. I'll look
into the other jobs tomorrow.

1438
02:01:52.708 --> 02:01:55.082
Thanks. Bye.
- Bye.

1439
02:02:00.625 --> 02:02:01.832
Rahul's done for.

1440
02:02:17.166 --> 02:02:19.082
Rahul? What are you doing here?
- Hi.

1441
02:02:19.916 --> 02:02:22.624
I have a friend in Khandala.
He's been asking me over for ages...

1442
02:02:22.708 --> 02:02:23.915
...but I've never had a chance to go.

1443
02:02:24.125 --> 02:02:26.665
And since we can't
work without you...

1444
02:02:26.750 --> 02:02:28.749
...I thought I'd meet him,
and give you a ride too.

1445
02:02:28.833 --> 02:02:31.540
As it is you're going alone,
so I thought you'd have company.

1446
02:02:32.208 --> 02:02:33.374
What are you staring at?
Hurry up, hop in.

1447
02:02:33.458 --> 02:02:35.290
If we go early we'll
beat the traffic. Come on.

1448
02:02:36.625 --> 02:02:39.499
Well, why are you smiling?

1449
02:02:39.750 --> 02:02:41.499
Nothing. Let's go.

1450
02:02:41.666 --> 02:02:44.124
Today I'm really
missing my friend. Really.

1451
02:03:02.416 --> 02:03:05.499
Tommy, Ceasar, quiet! Quiet!
- Pooja, I'm scared of dogs.

1452
02:03:05.583 --> 02:03:07.999
Pooja, Get them off me.
- They won't do anything.

1453
02:03:08.583 --> 02:03:11.665
Sister's taking a dance class there.
I'll just go and surprise her.

1454
02:03:11.958 --> 02:03:14.332
Stay here. Don't worry,
they won't bite you.

1455
02:03:14.416 --> 02:03:15.665
I'll be back.
- Sir Tommy, please.

1456
02:03:15.750 --> 02:03:18.790
Want some soft drink?
You can have these flowers too.

1457
02:03:31.166 --> 02:03:33.874
Sandhya, what are you doing?
I'll give you one now.

1458
02:03:34.333 --> 02:03:36.915
You've put on so much weight,
you can hardly move.

1459
02:03:37.291 --> 02:03:41.457
No more chocolates and ice creams
for you. Get it right this time.

1460
02:03:44.291 --> 02:03:46.957
Move the neck. Arms straight.

1461
02:03:47.166 --> 02:03:50.790
You... Why are you laughing?
Shut your mouth.

1462
02:03:51.541 --> 02:03:54.832
If anyone gets it wrong then
no one will watch TV tonight.

1463
02:03:55.000 --> 02:03:57.415
Don't come begging me again,
please sister.

1464
02:03:57.500 --> 02:03:59.457
Please Sister, let me watch TV.

1465
02:04:00.166 --> 02:04:02.457
Look. There comes your dear Pooja.

1466
02:04:03.208 --> 02:04:05.165
Sister, how did you recognise me?

1467
02:04:05.250 --> 02:04:07.165
There's no need to act smart.

1468
02:04:07.333 --> 02:04:09.665
I know all my girls from
the sound of their footsteps.

1469
02:04:10.125 --> 02:04:12.499
Happy Birthday to you!

1470
02:04:12.583 --> 02:04:15.499
What's this?
You've brought me another ugly saree.

1471
02:04:15.583 --> 02:04:17.790
Yes, I chose the ugliest
I could get my hands on.

1472
02:04:19.583 --> 02:04:22.124
Thank you.
- Go on, class is over.

1473
02:04:23.041 --> 02:04:26.915
Where you are going?
The class isn't over yet.

1474
02:04:27.000 --> 02:04:28.749
Now I'm here, and the class is over.

1475
02:04:29.125 --> 02:04:30.665
You're spoiling them rotten.

1476
02:04:30.750 --> 02:04:32.249
They behave well all year round.

1477
02:04:32.416 --> 02:04:34.415
And the moment you step here,
they start misbehaving.

1478
02:04:34.500 --> 02:04:35.999
Sometimes one should be spoilt.

1479
02:04:36.083 --> 02:04:41.665
No! Sir Tommy, No!
- What happened?

1480
02:04:41.750 --> 02:04:46.374
Tommy, no!
- Don't let him go! Nab him!

1481
02:04:46.458 --> 02:04:48.999
Sister! Wait!

1482
02:04:49.333 --> 02:04:50.874
He's Rahul, my friend.

1483
02:04:51.125 --> 02:04:52.249
Your friend?
- Yes!

1484
02:04:53.000 --> 02:04:54.999
Leave him, girls.
- Come on, leave him.

1485
02:04:55.083 --> 02:04:57.165
Tommy, Ceasar, go inside. Go.
- Tommy went?

1486
02:04:58.000 --> 02:04:59.665
They're gone.
Why are you so frightened?

1487
02:05:00.583 --> 02:05:02.874
Hi! Happy Birthday!

1488
02:05:04.791 --> 02:05:05.874
Ok.
- Where are your feet?

1489
02:05:06.791 --> 02:05:09.290
What are you up to?
- I'm trying to touch your feet.

1490
02:05:09.583 --> 02:05:13.207
Do I look that old?
- Not at all but out of respect.

1491
02:05:13.541 --> 02:05:14.790
Give me your hand.
- Pardon me?

1492
02:05:14.916 --> 02:05:16.249
Your hand.
- Yes.

1493
02:05:17.375 --> 02:05:18.457
Nice to meet you.

1494
02:05:19.250 --> 02:05:22.832
Oh, you've caught a cold.
Come, let's go in. - Yes, Pooja, please.

1495
02:05:22.916 --> 02:05:24.499
Save me from the dogs.
- They won't hurt you.

1496
02:05:24.583 --> 02:05:28.874
You don't know. They're very
dangerous. - Sister, who's he?

1497
02:05:29.875 --> 02:05:33.957
I don't know but
I'll have to find out.

1498
02:05:39.916 --> 02:05:43.207
Pooja, you didn't
tell me what Rahul does.

1499
02:05:43.416 --> 02:05:46.040
Rahul? He directs plays.

1500
02:05:46.250 --> 02:05:49.582
These days, I'm working with him.
- I see.

1501
02:05:51.333 --> 02:05:55.207
I think that you don't
like Rahul specially.

1502
02:05:55.291 --> 02:05:58.040
No, I like him very much.

1503
02:05:58.750 --> 02:05:59.999
Very much?

1504
02:06:00.125 --> 02:06:04.999
No, I mean to say,
he's a good friend.

1505
02:06:05.416 --> 02:06:10.624
Good friend?
You mean you don't love him.

1506
02:06:10.958 --> 02:06:16.207
Sister, Rahul's just a friend.
A dear friend.

1507
02:06:17.416 --> 02:06:21.124
I see... a dear friend.

1508
02:06:21.458 --> 02:06:23.790
It's not what you think...

1509
02:06:24.375 --> 02:06:26.457
...and in any case,
I wanted to tell you something.

1510
02:06:26.541 --> 02:06:30.207
There's no need to tell me.
I understand everything.

1511
02:06:30.291 --> 02:06:33.040
Stop it, Sister.
Sister, you've got it all wrong.

1512
02:06:33.125 --> 02:06:36.707
Pooja. Pooja.
- Rahul. Rahul.

1513
02:06:36.791 --> 02:06:40.124
Pooja.
- Rahul, what's up? - Hi!

1514
02:06:40.208 --> 02:06:41.624
Hi!
- What's up?

1515
02:06:41.958 --> 02:06:44.624
Nothing. Why are you standing
with the spoon? Come join us.

1516
02:06:45.708 --> 02:06:48.165
Stupid!
- Hey everybody!

1517
02:06:50.000 --> 02:06:52.249
Come on everyone, follow me... this way.

1518
02:06:53.333 --> 02:06:55.499
Okay. Come on.

1519
02:06:57.083 --> 02:06:59.124
If it's not love, then what is it?

1520
02:07:00.750 --> 02:07:04.624
Sister... honestly!
- Look here, girl!

1521
02:07:05.208 --> 02:07:07.832
I've known you since you
were twelve years old.

1522
02:07:08.458 --> 02:07:14.124
What your heart doesn't
let you know, it tells me.

1523
02:07:14.833 --> 02:07:18.999
The look in your eyes says
that you love this boy very much.

1524
02:07:19.208 --> 02:07:23.499
Now stop lying to me.
Understood? Okay?

1525
02:07:24.083 --> 02:07:25.499
"Just a dear friend".

1526
02:07:26.458 --> 02:07:27.665
Listen, Sister...

1527
02:07:40.208 --> 02:07:46.249
"I can't recollect
when this happened."

1528
02:07:46.958 --> 02:07:52.582
"It's become difficult to
hide this secret from everyone."

1529
02:07:53.583 --> 02:08:00.249
"If you say so,
today I'll ask God for something."

1530
02:08:00.375 --> 02:08:06.790
"Oh dear, what's going on?
- I don't really know."

1531
02:08:07.041 --> 02:08:13.582
"What this leads to...
- Let it become a romance."

1532
02:08:35.750 --> 02:08:40.415
So when is Ajay coming back?

1533
02:08:41.125 --> 02:08:43.665
Nothing is definite, but
he could come at any time.

1534
02:08:43.750 --> 02:08:47.665
Say D.
- D.

1535
02:08:47.750 --> 02:08:49.749
Say O.
- O.

1536
02:08:49.833 --> 02:08:52.249
Say N.
- N.

1537
02:08:52.333 --> 02:08:54.499
Say K.
- K. - Yes.

1538
02:08:54.583 --> 02:08:56.624
Now say E.
- E.

1539
02:08:56.833 --> 02:08:59.540
Say Y.
- Y. - I'll be right back.

1540
02:08:59.625 --> 02:09:01.999
Alright. Very good. Very good.

1541
02:09:02.083 --> 02:09:03.207
Let's start all over again.

1542
02:09:03.291 --> 02:09:05.457
D.
- D.

1543
02:09:06.250 --> 02:09:08.457
Okay, okay.

1544
02:09:09.958 --> 02:09:15.415
D. O. N.
- N.

1545
02:09:16.125 --> 02:09:20.290
K.
- Pooja, give me your hand. - Why?

1546
02:09:20.875 --> 02:09:22.915
I won't hit you! Give me your hand.

1547
02:09:24.000 --> 02:09:25.124
Here it is.

1548
02:09:26.458 --> 02:09:27.540
Here.

1549
02:09:27.625 --> 02:09:29.415
What's this?
- Hush.

1550
02:09:30.625 --> 02:09:33.415
Listen carefully to what
I'm going to tell you.

1551
02:09:34.583 --> 02:09:36.540
Ever since you were a child...

1552
02:09:37.541 --> 02:09:41.499
...you've always put
others before yourself.

1553
02:09:43.000 --> 02:09:46.374
I've always been
overwhelmed by your behavior.

1554
02:09:47.750 --> 02:09:51.874
But today this same
behaviour has made me sad.

1555
02:09:53.333 --> 02:09:54.582
But I...
- Quiet!

1556
02:09:55.375 --> 02:09:58.749
Sometimes, it's very important
to think of oneself, Pooja.

1557
02:10:00.583 --> 02:10:04.624
I see that you are
running away from your dreams.

1558
02:10:05.500 --> 02:10:07.249
You won't let them come true.

1559
02:10:08.833 --> 02:10:10.499
Don't do this, Pooja.

1560
02:10:11.583 --> 02:10:17.290
Not everybody is fortunate to
have their dreams come true.

1561
02:10:18.333 --> 02:10:19.457
Don't do this.

1562
02:10:21.500 --> 02:10:25.540
Let me tell you something.
One can fall in love many times.

1563
02:10:27.250 --> 02:10:30.165
True love only happens once.

1564
02:10:34.000 --> 02:10:36.249
The step you're unable to take...

1565
02:10:37.500 --> 02:10:42.040
...Lord Ganpati will help you.

1566
02:10:43.041 --> 02:10:44.874
He'll show you the right path.

1567
02:10:45.666 --> 02:10:49.040
He'll give you the strength
to fulfill your dreams.

1568
02:10:51.375 --> 02:10:53.332
Keep Him with you always.

1569
02:10:54.208 --> 02:10:55.874
I have faith in Him.

1570
02:10:57.250 --> 02:10:58.749
The Lord will set everything right.

1571
02:11:00.291 --> 02:11:01.374
I love you, Sister.

1572
02:11:04.208 --> 02:11:06.374
Stop it!

1573
02:11:06.875 --> 02:11:10.624
I don't want to make
a habit of crying.

1574
02:11:12.750 --> 02:11:13.832
Pooja!

1575
02:11:16.583 --> 02:11:17.665
No.

1576
02:11:17.791 --> 02:11:19.457
No way.

1577
02:11:19.750 --> 02:11:22.332
You are very fat. Sister will
scold me if I give this to you.

1578
02:11:24.208 --> 02:11:26.665
Why are you frightened?
- Pardon me?

1579
02:11:27.000 --> 02:11:29.374
Why are you frightened of
being in love? Tell her.

1580
02:11:29.833 --> 02:11:31.499
Love and me? I was just...

1581
02:11:31.583 --> 02:11:32.665
Okay, give me your hand.

1582
02:11:33.250 --> 02:11:34.374
Give me your hand.

1583
02:11:35.375 --> 02:11:36.499
Nice to meet you.

1584
02:11:38.416 --> 02:11:39.499
Take it!

1585
02:11:40.083 --> 02:11:42.082
What's this?
- This is, in a way, my blessing.

1586
02:11:42.583 --> 02:11:44.374
I'm very stingy in such matters.

1587
02:11:44.458 --> 02:11:46.832
I don't give my
blessing that easily.

1588
02:11:47.333 --> 02:11:51.540
But when I saw you I thought
that perhaps you need it.

1589
02:11:52.583 --> 02:11:56.457
This will help you to say
what you're unable to say.

1590
02:11:57.666 --> 02:11:59.082
Keep it very carefully.

1591
02:12:00.250 --> 02:12:02.499
You get it?
- Got it.

1592
02:12:02.583 --> 02:12:04.874
Bye.
- Bye. - She's on her way.

1593
02:12:05.333 --> 02:12:08.290
If you can't say it,
then I'll say it... - I'll say it.

1594
02:12:08.375 --> 02:12:10.415
Definitely?
- Definitely.

1595
02:12:11.750 --> 02:12:13.290
Okay.
- Okay.

1596
02:12:18.666 --> 02:12:19.957
Mark my words carefully.

1597
02:12:28.375 --> 02:12:30.499
Bye!
- Bye.

1598
02:12:30.583 --> 02:12:33.499
Bye!
- Good bye, Sister!

1599
02:12:33.583 --> 02:12:35.624
Bye!
- Bye, Sister!

1600
02:12:36.375 --> 02:12:40.874
Okay!

1601
02:12:41.250 --> 02:12:45.165
First, the bride. You can
drink straight from the bottle.

1602
02:12:48.625 --> 02:12:51.499
Okay. Here's to Soni and Jimmy.
Everyone together.

1603
02:12:51.583 --> 02:12:53.624
Cheers. For the most
beautiful couple I've seen.

1604
02:12:53.708 --> 02:12:54.874
And now I'm going to give a speech.

1605
02:12:54.958 --> 02:12:56.082
Excuse me.

1606
02:12:56.166 --> 02:13:01.415
Excuse me, ladies and gentlemen...
May I have your attention, please?

1607
02:13:01.583 --> 02:13:03.957
Aunty, please... thank you.

1608
02:13:07.708 --> 02:13:09.249
Since I am Jimmy's best man...

1609
02:13:09.333 --> 02:13:13.499
...it's my good fortune
to make a speech...

1610
02:13:14.458 --> 02:13:18.707
...and it's your misfortune
that you all have to listen to it.

1611
02:13:20.875 --> 02:13:23.249
Till today, I didn't understand
how two people can take a vow...

1612
02:13:23.333 --> 02:13:26.165
...to spend their entire
lives with each other.

1613
02:13:27.416 --> 02:13:30.624
I didn't believe in
these vows of marriage.

1614
02:13:30.958 --> 02:13:33.290
And seeing Jimmy and Soni together...

1615
02:13:33.375 --> 02:13:36.540
...only strengthened my conviction.

1616
02:13:36.958 --> 02:13:40.582
Because there can't be
anyone as innocent as Soni...

1617
02:13:41.458 --> 02:13:43.665
...and there can't be a
scamp to beat Jimmy.

1618
02:13:44.916 --> 02:13:48.290
I used to worry that Soni
and Jimmy are too different...

1619
02:13:48.375 --> 02:13:51.624
...to spend their lives together.

1620
02:13:53.541 --> 02:13:58.499
But today...
I realise that I was wrong.

1621
02:14:00.166 --> 02:14:02.290
I'm a little ashamed to admit...

1622
02:14:02.375 --> 02:14:06.249
...that I have started
believing in love.

1623
02:14:08.041 --> 02:14:11.540
The kind of love in which
lips don't speak...

1624
02:14:12.791 --> 02:14:14.540
...eyes do.

1625
02:14:16.291 --> 02:14:21.124
The kind of love that binds
two people together forever.

1626
02:14:23.583 --> 02:14:26.624
And today, I keep thinking
of just one thing.

1627
02:14:27.250 --> 02:14:29.332
I remember something...

1628
02:14:29.416 --> 02:14:33.665
...a very dear friend told me...

1629
02:14:33.958 --> 02:14:36.499
...about God.

1630
02:14:37.250 --> 02:14:41.249
God has already
brought hearts together...

1631
02:14:41.708 --> 02:14:43.457
...but then He left the hearts
to find each other.

1632
02:14:44.000 --> 02:14:46.249
He made us all in pairs.

1633
02:14:47.250 --> 02:14:50.749
For every one of us, somewhere,
there's one soul mate just for us.

1634
02:14:51.583 --> 02:14:54.165
He made Soni for Jimmy.

1635
02:14:54.875 --> 02:14:56.332
Today, to that God...

1636
02:14:56.416 --> 02:15:01.957
...I give thanks for
bringing Jimmy and Soni together.

1637
02:15:04.000 --> 02:15:05.082
And I pray that...

1638
02:15:06.125 --> 02:15:11.999
...He may give each one of us
the ability to recognise our soul mate.

1639
02:15:19.208 --> 02:15:21.540
Thank you.

1640
02:16:13.833 --> 02:16:15.165
My bangle?

1641
02:16:19.041 --> 02:16:21.207
Rahul, have you seen my bangle?

1642
02:16:23.166 --> 02:16:25.582
Darn! Now I'm sure I won't find it.

1643
02:16:26.791 --> 02:16:29.249
It was my favourite bangle.
- Mine, too.

1644
02:16:33.375 --> 02:16:34.540
Rahul!

1645
02:16:36.291 --> 02:16:37.374
Come on, give it to me.

1646
02:16:38.750 --> 02:16:39.999
Come here and take it.

1647
02:16:40.666 --> 02:16:41.790
What childish behavior!

1648
02:16:43.708 --> 02:16:44.832
Give it to me!

1649
02:16:45.583 --> 02:16:46.665
Come closer.

1650
02:16:48.708 --> 02:16:50.040
Here goes... happy?

1651
02:16:50.791 --> 02:16:51.874
Come closer.

1652
02:16:52.125 --> 02:16:54.624
Rahul!
- Closer...

1653
02:16:55.000 --> 02:16:56.082
Stop it!

1654
02:16:56.583 --> 02:17:43.624
Closer...

1655
02:18:57.583 --> 02:19:01.790
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1656
02:19:02.750 --> 02:19:08.040
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1657
02:19:12.958 --> 02:19:17.207
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1658
02:19:18.166 --> 02:19:22.457
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1659
02:19:23.333 --> 02:19:27.499
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1660
02:19:28.625 --> 02:19:33.624
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1661
02:19:33.708 --> 02:19:38.165
"We'd rather have died
than reveal our secret."

1662
02:19:38.666 --> 02:19:43.832
"Oh, my love."

1663
02:19:43.958 --> 02:19:48.040
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1664
02:19:49.125 --> 02:19:54.374
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1665
02:20:35.541 --> 02:20:51.124
"You were a few steps away from me.
I, a few steps away from you."

1666
02:20:51.208 --> 02:20:56.207
"Yet we may as well have
been hundreds of miles apart"

1667
02:20:56.291 --> 02:21:00.915
"Step by step
our wavering hearts came together."

1668
02:21:01.208 --> 02:21:03.874
"Oh, my love."

1669
02:21:03.958 --> 02:21:06.415
"Oh, my love"

1670
02:21:06.500 --> 02:21:10.540
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1671
02:21:11.625 --> 02:21:16.082
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1672
02:21:16.833 --> 02:21:20.957
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1673
02:21:22.000 --> 02:21:27.290
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1674
02:22:08.458 --> 02:22:23.957
"Come, you have won me over
and I am defeated by my heart."

1675
02:22:24.041 --> 02:22:28.874
"Today, with great difficulty
my lips say love."

1676
02:22:28.958 --> 02:22:31.790
"Now I'm wildly in love..."

1677
02:22:31.875 --> 02:22:33.832
"...don't ever leave me..."

1678
02:22:34.333 --> 02:22:38.957
"...don't ever leave me, my love."

1679
02:22:39.333 --> 02:22:43.582
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something"

1680
02:22:44.416 --> 02:22:48.957
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1681
02:22:49.708 --> 02:22:53.749
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1682
02:22:54.916 --> 02:22:59.415
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1683
02:22:59.916 --> 02:23:04.457
"We would rather have died
than reveal our secret."

1684
02:23:05.041 --> 02:23:10.249
"Oh, my love."

1685
02:23:10.333 --> 02:23:14.374
"How long shall we sit in silence?
We both want to say something."

1686
02:23:15.416 --> 02:23:21.207
"You say something,
I'll say something, my love."

1687
02:24:11.041 --> 02:24:15.290
Careful. Hey, Suppandi,
watch the scenery. Jimmy, watch Soni.

1688
02:24:15.375 --> 02:24:18.707
What's up, Supandi? Tell me.

1689
02:24:18.791 --> 02:24:20.415
Oh.
- I'm coming. I'm coming.

1690
02:24:20.500 --> 02:24:22.124
Just do this for me.

1691
02:24:22.208 --> 02:24:25.915
How much do I work tell me?
- Keep this on top.

1692
02:24:26.000 --> 02:24:28.332
Take it. - Where's Pooja?
She's nowhere to be seen.

1693
02:24:51.125 --> 02:24:52.207
Rahul!

1694
02:24:53.750 --> 02:24:54.874
The set is ready.

1695
02:24:56.208 --> 02:24:57.374
Good, well done.

1696
02:24:58.500 --> 02:24:59.707
Call Pooja.
- Okay.

1697
02:25:00.250 --> 02:25:01.832
Shruti. Call Pooja.
- Yes!

1698
02:25:09.333 --> 02:25:10.999
Pooja, we're ready.

1699
02:25:14.625 --> 02:25:16.874
Are you angry with me?
- Not at all.

1700
02:25:19.708 --> 02:25:21.165
Then why aren't you speaking to me?

1701
02:25:21.666 --> 02:25:22.749
I am speaking to you.

1702
02:25:24.583 --> 02:25:28.707
For three days, I haven't seen
your face or heard your voice.

1703
02:25:29.583 --> 02:25:31.665
I was very busy.

1704
02:25:31.750 --> 02:25:33.624
I have been calling you everyday.

1705
02:25:34.041 --> 02:25:35.207
Why haven't you been answering?

1706
02:25:36.083 --> 02:25:38.457
The phone has been out
of order for some time.

1707
02:25:50.083 --> 02:25:51.165
What is the problem?

1708
02:25:53.583 --> 02:25:56.915
Tell me. I want to know the
cause of your restlessness.

1709
02:25:58.166 --> 02:26:01.249
There's no problem.
- There is a problem.

1710
02:26:02.375 --> 02:26:03.540
Serious problem.

1711
02:26:05.375 --> 02:26:10.332
The fact is that we both
love each other very much.

1712
02:26:12.541 --> 02:26:14.832
We can't tell each other about it.

1713
02:26:18.708 --> 02:26:21.749
Today, I've come here to tell you...

1714
02:26:25.125 --> 02:26:26.540
...that I love you.

1715
02:26:28.041 --> 02:26:29.249
I love you very much.

1716
02:26:30.916 --> 02:26:33.540
And I know that you also love me.

1717
02:26:33.833 --> 02:26:34.915
So then, say it once...

1718
02:26:36.125 --> 02:26:40.124
...and that will be the
end of your restlessness.

1719
02:26:41.458 --> 02:26:42.624
Everything will be all right.

1720
02:26:45.958 --> 02:26:48.207
I don't love you.
- You're lying.

1721
02:26:48.291 --> 02:26:51.415
I'm not lying.
- You aren't?

1722
02:26:52.541 --> 02:26:55.957
Look into my eyes and tell me...

1723
02:26:56.541 --> 02:26:59.707
...that we weren't
made for each other.

1724
02:27:01.458 --> 02:27:02.540
We weren't.

1725
02:27:03.375 --> 02:27:08.207
Tell me that when I leave you,
you don't turn to look at me.

1726
02:27:09.583 --> 02:27:10.665
I don't.

1727
02:27:11.625 --> 02:27:16.415
Tell me that nothing happens
to you when I touch you.

1728
02:27:19.333 --> 02:27:20.915
Nothing.
- Tell me...

1729
02:27:23.083 --> 02:27:25.332
...that you don't want to
come into my arms right now.

1730
02:27:28.291 --> 02:27:29.415
I don't.

1731
02:27:29.750 --> 02:27:31.582
Look into my eyes just once...

1732
02:27:33.166 --> 02:27:35.540
...and tell me that
you don't love me.

1733
02:27:40.500 --> 02:27:41.582
I don't...

1734
02:27:43.083 --> 02:27:52.415
"For each other."
- I don't...

1735
02:27:52.500 --> 02:27:56.332
I don't...

1736
02:27:56.500 --> 02:27:58.624
Terrific performance!
Very well done!

1737
02:27:59.000 --> 02:28:01.915
Excellent!
Fabulous Rahul! Wonderful.

1738
02:28:02.000 --> 02:28:03.249
Fantastic. - Thank you, buddy.

1739
02:28:03.333 --> 02:28:05.249
Rahul, there was no problem
with my lighting, was there?

1740
02:28:05.333 --> 02:28:07.374
Soni, I'd told you.
- Nisha!

1741
02:28:08.041 --> 02:28:11.915
Nisha.? Let's go and give her
a warm welcome. - Welcome.

1742
02:28:12.333 --> 02:28:14.957
Hi.
- Hi! Great to see you back again.

1743
02:28:15.291 --> 02:28:16.374
Hi.
- Hi.

1744
02:28:16.458 --> 02:28:18.874
Oh, Raju, I'd told you
she'd come back soon. - Hi.

1745
02:28:21.333 --> 02:28:24.540
'But I'm sure that
when I'm not here...'

1746
02:28:24.625 --> 02:28:26.832
'... you'll remember me often...'

1747
02:28:26.958 --> 02:28:30.124
'... and I don't know why,
but when I get back...'

1748
02:28:30.208 --> 02:28:35.915
'... you'll be on your knees
begging me to marry you.'

1749
02:28:36.041 --> 02:28:38.624
'And then perhaps I may not
be in the mood for marrying.'

1750
02:28:42.625 --> 02:28:44.290
Well, I'll be off.

1751
02:28:44.375 --> 02:28:47.457
I'm a little tired.
I'll see you all tomorrow.

1752
02:28:47.708 --> 02:28:49.582
Okay. As you wish.
- Bye.

1753
02:28:51.083 --> 02:28:54.165
What's up with Nisha?
- She's tired. She'll come tomorrow.

1754
02:28:54.250 --> 02:28:55.749
Don't get unnecessarily worried.

1755
02:29:24.875 --> 02:29:26.457
I'm not a nice girl, Rahul.

1756
02:29:29.583 --> 02:29:30.665
I'm bad.

1757
02:29:33.166 --> 02:29:34.374
I'm really bad.

1758
02:29:35.625 --> 02:29:39.290
No Nisha, you're my friend.

1759
02:29:40.541 --> 02:29:43.624
And no friend of mine is bad.

1760
02:29:44.958 --> 02:29:47.874
No, Rahul, you don't know...

1761
02:29:49.500 --> 02:29:50.874
...that I'm not a nice girl.

1762
02:29:52.625 --> 02:29:53.707
Now you see...

1763
02:29:54.916 --> 02:29:59.124
...I love a boy...

1764
02:30:00.791 --> 02:30:02.749
...and have always loved him...

1765
02:30:04.666 --> 02:30:08.874
...and today I realised
that he doesn't love me.

1766
02:30:10.125 --> 02:30:11.790
He loves someone else.

1767
02:30:13.791 --> 02:30:15.540
I feel bad...

1768
02:30:17.083 --> 02:30:18.165
I'm hurt...

1769
02:30:19.333 --> 02:30:22.165
I'm upset. I feel jealous.

1770
02:30:25.291 --> 02:30:27.290
Rahul, I shouldn't feel like this.

1771
02:30:29.000 --> 02:30:30.082
I'm bad.

1772
02:30:31.500 --> 02:30:32.582
I'm very bad.

1773
02:30:33.833 --> 02:30:36.415
No, Nisha...
- No, Rahul.

1774
02:30:38.333 --> 02:30:43.165
Actually, that boy
isn't just the one I love...

1775
02:30:44.875 --> 02:30:47.124
...but he's also my best friend.

1776
02:30:49.416 --> 02:30:54.165
Today, for the first time,
I saw love in his eyes.

1777
02:30:56.250 --> 02:30:58.915
I couldn't bring that love
in all these years...

1778
02:31:00.458 --> 02:31:02.457
...but that other girl has.

1779
02:31:04.583 --> 02:31:08.999
Perhaps they are
made for each other.

1780
02:31:11.416 --> 02:31:13.374
Perhaps I was never meant for him.

1781
02:31:15.625 --> 02:31:17.790
Perhaps her love for him is true.

1782
02:31:19.833 --> 02:31:24.624
So you see, I should be
happy for my friend.

1783
02:31:25.791 --> 02:31:27.999
I should revel in his happiness.

1784
02:31:30.041 --> 02:31:34.624
But I'm not happy... I'm not!

1785
02:31:36.291 --> 02:31:37.499
I'm very bad...

1786
02:31:38.708 --> 02:31:39.790
...really very bad.

1787
02:31:40.666 --> 02:31:43.915
Nisha, you're not bad...

1788
02:31:45.416 --> 02:31:46.665
...you're really nice.

1789
02:31:49.083 --> 02:31:50.415
You know who is bad?

1790
02:31:54.375 --> 02:31:55.582
He is bad...

1791
02:31:58.083 --> 02:32:01.249
The One who plays around
with us mortals...

1792
02:32:03.791 --> 02:32:06.082
...making A love B...

1793
02:32:07.583 --> 02:32:09.082
...while B loves C...

1794
02:32:10.541 --> 02:32:12.124
...and C loves D.

1795
02:32:14.291 --> 02:32:16.082
I don't know why He does this.

1796
02:32:17.958 --> 02:32:20.707
When He makes one
person love another...

1797
02:32:22.000 --> 02:32:24.874
...He ought to make sure that the
other one also loves her in return.

1798
02:32:26.958 --> 02:32:28.040
Right?

1799
02:32:33.291 --> 02:32:34.707
But that's not what He does.

1800
02:32:36.791 --> 02:32:40.540
He's really bad.

1801
02:32:41.958 --> 02:32:43.040
You're not bad.

1802
02:32:45.041 --> 02:32:47.540
He's bad.

1803
02:32:48.458 --> 02:32:52.540
You're right... It's He who's bad.

1804
02:32:54.625 --> 02:32:55.957
He's bad!

1805
02:32:58.291 --> 02:33:00.207
You're bad. I'm not.

1806
02:33:01.125 --> 02:33:03.707
You're bad. I haven't
done anything wrong.

1807
02:33:03.916 --> 02:33:06.707
You are the one.

1808
02:33:07.166 --> 02:33:12.332
You are bad. You are bad.

1809
02:33:13.166 --> 02:33:14.249
I'm not bad.

1810
02:33:15.333 --> 02:33:17.249
I'm not bad.
- I'm sorry, Nisha.

1811
02:33:24.166 --> 02:33:25.582
Don't say sorry, Rahul.

1812
02:33:27.125 --> 02:33:28.207
Else, I'll cry.

1813
02:33:30.333 --> 02:33:36.332
I'm sorry, Nisha.
- Don't say sorry, I'll cry.

1814
02:33:37.500 --> 02:33:38.582
Sorry.

1815
02:33:39.750 --> 02:33:43.999
No, Rahul, don't say sorry.

1816
02:33:44.541 --> 02:33:45.707
I'll break down.

1817
02:33:48.250 --> 02:33:49.332
Rahul!

1818
02:34:04.625 --> 02:34:05.707
Ajay...

1819
02:34:07.125 --> 02:34:12.290
...when I was a little girl, you
used to tease me about my dreams.

1820
02:34:14.208 --> 02:34:19.707
When I used to tell you that I am
looking for the one meant for me...

1821
02:34:21.875 --> 02:34:24.665
...you would say that
I am crazy and silly.

1822
02:34:26.375 --> 02:34:29.999
You'd say that when I grow up...

1823
02:34:31.375 --> 02:34:32.957
...my dreams will vanish.

1824
02:34:35.041 --> 02:34:38.332
But you know, I have grown up...

1825
02:34:40.000 --> 02:34:41.707
...and my dreams have not vanished.

1826
02:34:42.916 --> 02:34:46.707
They have grown with me.

1827
02:34:48.333 --> 02:34:51.415
That day, at the airport, when you
suddenly asked me to marry you...

1828
02:34:52.625 --> 02:34:54.957
...at first I didn't
realise what I should do.

1829
02:34:56.416 --> 02:34:58.040
Then I saw you going.

1830
02:34:59.708 --> 02:35:02.415
But then I thought, I was crazy...

1831
02:35:04.166 --> 02:35:05.832
...you were my dearest friend...

1832
02:35:07.083 --> 02:35:12.749
...and the one who knew me the most.

1833
02:35:13.750 --> 02:35:15.290
Who could be better for me?

1834
02:35:16.833 --> 02:35:20.124
And I was standing
lost in my thoughts.

1835
02:35:22.625 --> 02:35:27.082
You left, and silly me
made you a part of my dreams.

1836
02:35:28.458 --> 02:35:32.374
I started believing that
you were the one made for me.

1837
02:35:34.625 --> 02:35:35.707
And then...

1838
02:35:37.166 --> 02:35:40.082
...and then I met Rahul.

1839
02:35:40.750 --> 02:35:43.082
You're marrying Pooja?

1840
02:35:44.000 --> 02:35:45.165
What are you saying Ajay?

1841
02:35:45.625 --> 02:35:47.832
But Pooja hasn't said
anything to me about it.

1842
02:35:47.958 --> 02:35:50.082
I had forbidden her
from telling you.

1843
02:35:50.625 --> 02:35:52.665
I wanted to tell you myself.

1844
02:35:52.958 --> 02:35:54.874
Oh, God! I can hardly believe you!

1845
02:35:55.333 --> 02:35:57.749
I'm so happy! When are you coming?

1846
02:35:57.833 --> 02:36:00.374
I called just to tell you this.

1847
02:36:00.875 --> 02:36:02.415
I'm coming tomorrow.
- Tomorrow?

1848
02:36:02.791 --> 02:36:04.790
What can I tell you about Rahul?

1849
02:36:06.083 --> 02:36:07.165
Where do I begin?

1850
02:36:08.583 --> 02:36:13.957
Well, you should realise that
I've never met anyone like him.

1851
02:36:15.916 --> 02:36:19.124
Sometimes he's an angel,
sometimes a devil.

1852
02:36:20.500 --> 02:36:23.165
Sometimes crazy...
and sometimes a genius.

1853
02:36:24.500 --> 02:36:26.207
Sometimes he scolds so harshly...

1854
02:36:27.333 --> 02:36:29.832
...and sometimes he makes
funny faces to make me laugh.

1855
02:36:31.958 --> 02:36:34.082
At times he's more
stubborn than a child...

1856
02:36:35.500 --> 02:36:37.332
...and at times he's
a beloved companion.

1857
02:36:37.708 --> 02:36:39.290
In three days? Oh, no.

1858
02:36:39.541 --> 02:36:42.790
I want time to get things
ready for a big wedding.

1859
02:36:43.041 --> 02:36:44.415
Mom, I don't have time.

1860
02:36:44.500 --> 02:36:47.207
The company's sending
me to Japan for a year.

1861
02:36:47.333 --> 02:36:49.999
You'll have to wait for eight
to ten months. Think about it.

1862
02:36:50.083 --> 02:36:52.374
I can't wait that long.

1863
02:36:52.666 --> 02:36:55.457
All right, you come here,
and I'll start the preparations.

1864
02:36:55.541 --> 02:36:57.790
The dreams of your crazy girl
have come true, Ajay.

1865
02:36:59.500 --> 02:37:01.415
She's found the
partner of her dreams...

1866
02:37:04.208 --> 02:37:06.624
...and she wants to know whether...

1867
02:37:06.708 --> 02:37:11.582
...she can make
all her dreams come true.

1868
02:37:14.041 --> 02:37:16.457
Can she make her dreams come true?

1869
02:37:43.750 --> 02:37:45.124
Ajay phoned just now.

1870
02:37:46.375 --> 02:37:48.207
He's told me everything.

1871
02:37:49.375 --> 02:37:50.874
He's coming tomorrow, Pooja...

1872
02:37:51.916 --> 02:37:54.374
...and he says to get the wedding
organised as quickly as possible.

1873
02:37:55.916 --> 02:37:59.874
You're a silly goose. You would
tell me your smallest secrets...

1874
02:38:00.583 --> 02:38:02.374
...and you hid such
a big one from me?

1875
02:38:04.250 --> 02:38:05.374
Come here...

1876
02:38:09.000 --> 02:38:10.082
...sit by my side.

1877
02:38:17.500 --> 02:38:20.832
You know, Pooja, ever since
you came to this house...

1878
02:38:21.666 --> 02:38:23.707
...l've had a dream in which...

1879
02:38:23.791 --> 02:38:26.082
...one day, you'd become
my daughter-in-law...

1880
02:38:26.916 --> 02:38:31.457
...and I, your mother.

1881
02:38:33.333 --> 02:38:34.415
But I was afraid...

1882
02:38:35.208 --> 02:38:37.290
...of how you two would
be when you grew up.

1883
02:38:38.125 --> 02:38:39.832
Whether you would be friends.

1884
02:38:40.541 --> 02:38:42.040
Whether you'd take a
liking to each other.

1885
02:38:42.958 --> 02:38:46.374
Hence, I never revealed
my heart's desire.

1886
02:38:47.125 --> 02:38:48.707
I also wanted that...

1887
02:38:48.791 --> 02:38:51.707
...you should decide,
if at all you wanted it...

1888
02:38:51.791 --> 02:38:53.165
...but not for my sake.

1889
02:38:54.125 --> 02:38:59.040
I wanted you to choose Ajay
out of your own free will.

1890
02:39:00.000 --> 02:39:06.082
You don't know how happy I am,
for I know...

1891
02:39:06.833 --> 02:39:08.749
...that there cannot be
a better girl...

1892
02:39:08.833 --> 02:39:12.499
...than you for my son.

1893
02:39:13.416 --> 02:39:18.165
Just watch. I'm going to
give you a grand wedding.

1894
02:39:19.416 --> 02:39:24.499
You have no idea how happy I am.

1895
02:39:27.250 --> 02:39:28.332
May you live long.

1896
02:40:31.833 --> 02:40:33.540
I want full lights
and I want to see...

1897
02:40:33.625 --> 02:40:35.374
...M6 on both left
and right of stage.

1898
02:40:35.750 --> 02:40:37.999
Suppandi, in a while I
want to hear the music tracks.

1899
02:40:38.333 --> 02:40:42.415
Soni, the elevation
should be three feet higher...

1900
02:40:42.541 --> 02:40:44.665
...or else the audience on stage right
will not know what is going on.

1901
02:40:44.958 --> 02:40:46.832
When Ballu lights M6, one spotlight
will filter here on this side...

1902
02:40:46.916 --> 02:40:49.332
...and the audience gets a glimpse
of the entry before it happens.

1903
02:40:49.416 --> 02:40:51.249
Rahul.
- Hi Pooja.

1904
02:40:51.416 --> 02:40:52.915
You just make sure
this doesn't happen.

1905
02:40:53.000 --> 02:40:54.415
I want them in complete...
- Rahul.

1906
02:40:54.750 --> 02:40:56.457
Sure. Sure.
- I'll take care of it. - Yes.

1907
02:40:57.916 --> 02:41:00.040
I need to talk to you.

1908
02:41:00.416 --> 02:41:02.624
The show opens in two days,
we'll talk later.

1909
02:41:02.708 --> 02:41:05.290
Shruti. Soni, you just take
care of this. I'll see you.

1910
02:41:05.708 --> 02:41:06.790
Hello.

1911
02:41:07.875 --> 02:41:10.332
Show me all the costumes of
act three's dream sequence.

1912
02:41:10.458 --> 02:41:13.457
Always sitting with Soni.
Never does any work. - That's not so.

1913
02:41:14.291 --> 02:41:15.665
All are approved?
- Yes, this one's approved.

1914
02:41:15.750 --> 02:41:17.374
Yes.
- Trials done? - Yes. - Rahul.

1915
02:41:17.958 --> 02:41:20.290
Yes.
- Rahul, I have to talk to you.

1916
02:41:20.375 --> 02:41:22.415
Pooja, just a minute.
I'll just finish this... - But...

1917
02:41:22.500 --> 02:41:26.082
One minute. One minute.
Shruti. Shruti, pay attention here.

1918
02:41:28.875 --> 02:41:31.207
Okay... tell me,
what's the problem? Shoot.

1919
02:41:31.875 --> 02:41:35.374
Rahul, please try and understand
what I am about to tell you.

1920
02:41:35.458 --> 02:41:39.040
Rahul, Nisha's calling you. There's
a call from the auditorium. - Darn.

1921
02:41:39.125 --> 02:41:40.249
I forgot to talk to her.
I'll be right back.

1922
02:41:40.333 --> 02:41:41.415
Supandi you come with me... - Rahul.

1923
02:41:41.541 --> 02:41:42.624
Where's Nisha?

1924
02:41:46.625 --> 02:41:48.124
Rahul, please be serious...

1925
02:41:49.083 --> 02:41:50.165
Ajay?

1926
02:41:50.500 --> 02:41:54.082
My name is Ajay, but if you
like you can call me Rahul.

1927
02:41:55.000 --> 02:42:00.249
Fatso! I love you!
- Nisha, you'd said...

1928
02:42:02.833 --> 02:42:04.540
I really missed you.

1929
02:42:07.416 --> 02:42:11.832
Remember Pooja, I told you that
I'd come to get you anytime any day?

1930
02:42:12.166 --> 02:42:13.249
Here I am.

1931
02:42:13.833 --> 02:42:17.165
I came here after meeting mom.
She is so elated.

1932
02:42:18.375 --> 02:42:21.290
Hey, I hope you haven't
changed your mind.

1933
02:42:21.583 --> 02:42:22.665
You're marrying me, aren't you?

1934
02:42:24.166 --> 02:42:25.457
Have you told your friends?

1935
02:42:25.833 --> 02:42:29.374
I was going to... - Hear that!
I'll have to do that, too?

1936
02:42:29.458 --> 02:42:32.790
Come on. I'll tell them all
that we are getting married.

1937
02:42:33.375 --> 02:42:37.665
Ladies and gentlemen...
I'm sorry for the intrusion.

1938
02:42:38.166 --> 02:42:41.457
You don't know my name. It's Ajay.

1939
02:42:43.208 --> 02:42:45.040
I'm Pooja's childhood friend.

1940
02:42:46.416 --> 02:42:48.707
And since she hasn't
found a worthy guy...

1941
02:42:49.458 --> 02:42:52.207
...I took pity on her,
and I'm going to marry her.

1942
02:42:52.500 --> 02:42:55.415
Congratulations! - Alright, okay.
Thank you very much.

1943
02:42:55.500 --> 02:42:57.290
Congratulations!
- Thank you.

1944
02:42:59.458 --> 02:43:01.374
Thank you. Okay, okay.

1945
02:43:01.666 --> 02:43:02.999
In three days,
we're getting married.

1946
02:43:03.083 --> 02:43:05.332
...and you all must come,
with family.

1947
02:43:05.708 --> 02:43:07.040
Okay. Definitely.
- We'll all come.

1948
02:43:13.958 --> 02:43:15.040
Rahul!

1949
02:43:20.500 --> 02:43:24.707
Pooja, you're weird.
Why didn't you tell us before?

1950
02:43:24.916 --> 02:43:28.165
We had begun to feel
that you were our Maya.

1951
02:43:28.625 --> 02:43:32.124
We forgot you're Pooja,
and you have your own private life...

1952
02:43:32.666 --> 02:43:36.332
...and your own relationships
and even prior commitments.

1953
02:43:36.583 --> 02:43:38.540
We are really stupid!

1954
02:43:39.083 --> 02:43:42.540
Oh, I forgot...
Pooja, congratulations.

1955
02:43:43.500 --> 02:43:45.165
Thanks.
- And this is...

1956
02:43:46.625 --> 02:43:48.707
This is Rahul, our director.

1957
02:43:48.916 --> 02:43:51.915
Rahul, she likes your name a lot.

1958
02:43:52.083 --> 02:43:54.832
She likes only the name?
- I hope so, man!

1959
02:43:54.916 --> 02:43:56.332
Congratulations.
- Thank you.

1960
02:43:56.458 --> 02:43:59.374
Rahul, I have a request.
- Go on.

1961
02:43:59.458 --> 02:44:02.207
May I take her away for an hour?
- Oh, come on!

1962
02:44:02.541 --> 02:44:05.165
You're taking her
away forever from us.

1963
02:44:05.250 --> 02:44:08.582
That will be in a ceremonious way.
What say, Pooja?

1964
02:44:09.083 --> 02:44:12.999
This is just a lunch date with Pooja.
Do I have your permission?

1965
02:44:13.083 --> 02:44:14.749
My permission!

1966
02:44:15.041 --> 02:44:17.749
Now I'll have to get your
permission to meet Pooja.

1967
02:44:18.708 --> 02:44:20.040
Besides, now that you've come...

1968
02:44:20.125 --> 02:44:23.374
...Pooja won't be happy here,
will you Pooja?

1969
02:44:24.750 --> 02:44:27.874
So, go on. I'll get by without you.

1970
02:44:27.958 --> 02:44:30.874
Are you sure?
- Yes, of course! Absolutely!

1971
02:44:31.333 --> 02:44:33.457
You guys go and
have a good time. Go on.

1972
02:44:33.583 --> 02:44:36.665
We have his permission... let's go.
- Go on.

1973
02:44:36.750 --> 02:44:38.374
Okay guys.
- Okay, see you.

1974
02:44:38.708 --> 02:44:42.582
Bye. After three days, okay?
- We'll be there.

1975
02:44:58.750 --> 02:45:01.457
Ballu, show me the final mix.

1976
02:45:02.791 --> 02:45:05.832
Shruti, show me the sketches.

1977
02:45:07.333 --> 02:45:12.915
And Nisha, call up the
auditorium and tell them...

1978
02:45:14.500 --> 02:45:16.082
The thing is that...

1979
02:45:16.166 --> 02:45:17.707
...in two days we're
going on stage... - Rahul!

1980
02:45:33.583 --> 02:45:38.624
Lights! Why aren't you
showing me the lights.

1981
02:45:39.166 --> 02:45:41.832
There are just two days,
and you're taking it easy!

1982
02:45:42.208 --> 02:45:43.457
Come on, the lights.

1983
02:45:44.541 --> 02:45:45.665
Shruti, show me the sketches.

1984
02:45:46.041 --> 02:45:47.957
Quickly bring the
sketches here, fast!

1985
02:45:48.708 --> 02:45:51.040
Tania, hurry up with the band.

1986
02:45:51.541 --> 02:45:53.624
We've got to finish the
music rehearsals, too!

1987
02:45:53.708 --> 02:45:54.790
Come on, everybody.

1988
02:45:54.875 --> 02:45:56.832
Faster everybody. Come on.

1989
02:46:00.958 --> 02:46:02.332
This is our last meeting.

1990
02:46:04.125 --> 02:46:05.457
I'm getting married tomorrow.

1991
02:46:07.208 --> 02:46:10.874
I don't want to meet you
ever again after today.

1992
02:46:12.666 --> 02:46:16.332
Just assume that I was
never a part of your life.

1993
02:46:29.583 --> 02:46:33.457
As soon as I start to move,
track me with the spotlight...

1994
02:46:34.666 --> 02:46:37.415
...and the other will stay on Pooja.

1995
02:46:39.291 --> 02:46:41.249
When I get right up
to the audience...

1996
02:46:42.458 --> 02:46:44.707
...then slowly dim the light.

1997
02:46:46.791 --> 02:46:47.874
The show will be over...

1998
02:46:49.833 --> 02:46:50.915
The End.

1999
02:46:53.291 --> 02:46:54.374
That's it.

2000
02:46:54.833 --> 02:46:56.040
Any questions?

2001
02:46:56.375 --> 02:46:59.457
I don't want any mistakes, okay?
- Okay!

2002
02:46:59.541 --> 02:47:00.707
Raj, everything all right?
- Yes.

2003
02:47:01.083 --> 02:47:04.540
Okay then, tomorrow be
at the stadium on time.

2004
02:47:05.250 --> 02:47:06.707
Pack up?
- I'll take that. - All Right.

2005
02:47:06.916 --> 02:47:10.915
Hey, Rahul. Something
is bothering me. - What?

2006
02:47:11.458 --> 02:47:14.124
I don't like the end of your story.
- Why?

2007
02:47:15.333 --> 02:47:18.040
This ending's too sad.

2008
02:47:19.125 --> 02:47:21.665
A love story should
always have a happy ending.

2009
02:47:22.333 --> 02:47:25.290
The audience should
come out smiling, right?

2010
02:47:26.916 --> 02:47:29.082
People like to
live in a dream world.

2011
02:47:30.416 --> 02:47:31.999
They have seen many dreams...

2012
02:47:33.333 --> 02:47:35.082
...now let them see a little reality.

2013
02:47:36.791 --> 02:47:39.499
Every love story is
like this in real life.

2014
02:47:40.750 --> 02:47:44.999
Full of sorrow and pain.

2015
02:47:50.833 --> 02:47:53.874
No, Nisha. This ending
is absolutely right.

2016
02:47:55.708 --> 02:48:00.332
There can't be another
end to this love story.

2017
02:49:01.875 --> 02:49:05.665
"I know a girl, when she smiles..."

2018
02:49:06.208 --> 02:49:09.957
"...it rains."

2019
02:49:10.625 --> 02:49:14.582
"I know a boy, when he sings..."

2020
02:49:14.833 --> 02:49:18.749
"...it rains."

2021
02:49:35.083 --> 02:49:37.457
Jimmy, just go and check the
next entry stage left. - Okay.

2022
02:49:53.666 --> 02:49:57.249
The heart is crazy,
just refuses to listen.

2023
02:50:26.000 --> 02:50:32.124
"Oh dear, what's going on?
I don't really know."

2024
02:50:32.583 --> 02:50:39.082
"I only hope this does not
turn into a romance."

2025
02:50:39.166 --> 02:50:45.249
"Oh dear, what's going on?
I don't really know."

2026
02:50:45.750 --> 02:50:52.165
"But if this is a romance,
then so be it."

2027
02:51:32.666 --> 02:51:35.957
Pooja's last entry is after this.
Get her ready, and bring her here.

2028
02:51:36.083 --> 02:51:38.290
Don't worry. Nisha's getting
her ready, and bringing her.

2029
02:51:41.541 --> 02:51:42.624
Thanks.

2030
02:51:45.000 --> 02:51:46.582
Don't make this mistake, Pooja.

2031
02:51:49.125 --> 02:51:52.499
Very few people are lucky...

2032
02:51:52.583 --> 02:51:56.999
...enough to love and to be loved.

2033
02:51:59.541 --> 02:52:04.749
You can't break the tie
which He has ordained.

2034
02:52:06.375 --> 02:52:07.874
You can't break it.

2035
02:52:12.416 --> 02:52:18.040
I've spent my years giving
love the name of friendship.

2036
02:52:20.000 --> 02:52:23.457
Now, you're going to spend
the rest of your life...

2037
02:52:23.541 --> 02:52:27.207
...giving friendship
the name of love.

2038
02:52:28.708 --> 02:52:30.124
This is a betrayal!

2039
02:52:31.000 --> 02:52:34.332
A betrayal of love...
a betrayal of friendship.

2040
02:52:35.416 --> 02:52:36.832
Don't do such a thing!

2041
02:52:50.833 --> 02:52:52.249
This is our last meeting.

2042
02:52:53.750 --> 02:52:55.207
I'm getting married tomorrow.

2043
02:52:57.000 --> 02:52:59.874
I don't want to meet you
ever again after today.

2044
02:53:01.958 --> 02:53:04.624
Just assume that I was
never a part of your life.

2045
02:53:22.541 --> 02:53:25.374
I want to ask you
something before I go.

2046
02:53:28.791 --> 02:53:31.540
Did you ever love me...

2047
02:53:31.625 --> 02:53:37.582
...even for a single day
or a single moment?

2048
02:53:40.083 --> 02:53:43.415
This line is not in the play.
- Raju!

2049
02:53:44.250 --> 02:53:45.582
Tell me just once...

2050
02:53:47.000 --> 02:53:51.415
...have you ever really loved me?
Even for a moment?

2051
02:53:54.000 --> 02:53:56.415
What is Rahul saying?
- Shut up.

2052
02:54:02.000 --> 02:54:04.415
I won't leave without an
answer to this question.

2053
02:54:07.000 --> 02:54:08.582
I'm not going!

2054
02:54:11.458 --> 02:54:16.874
Did you ever love me,
even for a single moment?

2055
02:54:20.000 --> 02:54:21.915
No.
- What did you say?

2056
02:54:23.416 --> 02:54:24.582
I didn't hear that.

2057
02:54:25.833 --> 02:54:30.040
No.
- Speak up, I couldn't hear.

2058
02:54:32.041 --> 02:54:35.290
No.
- Louder, louder Pooja...

2059
02:54:35.375 --> 02:54:39.124
No, I've never loved you.

2060
02:54:40.625 --> 02:54:43.957
Not for a day, not for a moment.

2061
02:54:45.500 --> 02:54:46.582
Never.

2062
02:54:50.041 --> 02:54:51.624
That is all I wanted to hear.

2063
02:55:00.875 --> 02:55:05.415
Rahul... you'll remember
my name, won't you?

2064
02:55:29.666 --> 02:55:31.999
What can I tell you about Rahul?

2065
02:55:32.250 --> 02:55:33.665
Where do I begin?

2066
02:55:34.166 --> 02:55:39.540
Well, you should realise that
I've never met anyone like him.

2067
02:55:40.291 --> 02:55:43.540
Sometimes he's an angel,
sometimes, a devil.

2068
02:55:44.125 --> 02:55:47.124
Sometimes he's crazy,
sometimes he's a genius.

2069
02:55:47.958 --> 02:55:49.665
Sometimes, he scolds so harshly...

2070
02:55:49.750 --> 02:55:53.082
...and sometimes he makes
funny faces and makes me laugh.

2071
02:55:54.166 --> 02:55:56.707
At times he's more
stubborn than a child...

2072
02:55:56.791 --> 02:56:00.207
...and at times he's
a beloved companion.

2073
02:56:01.375 --> 02:56:06.707
What he is or is not,
I cannot really express in words...

2074
02:56:06.791 --> 02:56:11.207
...but I don't know why,
I feel that...

2075
02:56:30.166 --> 02:56:34.582
...when he looks at me,
I feel beautiful.

2076
02:56:36.750 --> 02:56:40.749
When he laughs, I feel like dancing.

2077
02:56:41.500 --> 02:56:45.165
When he's upset, I feel like
holding him in my arms.

2078
02:56:45.750 --> 02:56:49.582
When he loves me,
my eyes fill with tears.

2079
02:56:51.583 --> 02:56:53.749
He's made me realise...

2080
02:56:53.833 --> 02:56:58.165
...that I am made for him...
and he for me.

2081
02:57:00.333 --> 02:57:02.415
I love him very much...

2082
02:57:03.916 --> 02:57:07.540
...not for one day or one moment...

2083
02:57:09.041 --> 02:57:10.540
...but for my whole life.

2084
02:57:12.791 --> 02:57:15.790
I love you, Rahul. I love you.

2085
02:57:43.666 --> 02:57:44.749
Yes.

2086
02:57:45.416 --> 02:57:46.457
Rahul!

2087
02:57:49.375 --> 02:57:52.790
Now that I've seen them,
I believe that someone, somewhere...

2088
02:57:52.875 --> 02:57:53.957
...was made for me as well.

2089
02:57:55.375 --> 02:57:57.124
Isn't that so?
- Yes.

2090
02:58:00.083 --> 02:58:02.499
My name is Ajay. Yours?

2091
02:58:02.583 --> 02:58:05.082
I'm Nisha.
- Nisha!

2092
02:58:06.416 --> 02:58:09.082
Are you married?
- What?

2093
02:58:25.666 --> 02:58:34.624
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."

2094
02:58:34.875 --> 02:58:43.374
"It brings along sleepless nights.
It steals sleep and solace."

2095
02:58:43.625 --> 02:58:47.332
"It shows them the path of love."

2096
02:58:47.416 --> 02:58:51.624
"It brings joy and tears."

2097
02:58:51.708 --> 02:58:53.540
"The heart is crazy."

2098
02:58:53.875 --> 02:58:55.624
"The heart is besotted."

2099
02:58:55.875 --> 02:58:58.124
"The heart is crazy."

2100
02:58:58.208 --> 02:59:00.957
"The heart is besotted."

2101
02:59:01.041 --> 02:59:09.415
"The heart is crazy,
the heart is besotted."
